{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 01:32:19", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8d42356e-b89d-4f5f-93cd-3235264c851f', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Agent Tasks UI Enhancement"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XFiNxgxdf9oehyhcrNxvcT', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XFiNxgxdf9oehyhcrNxvcT', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Agent Tasks UI Enhancement - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nEnhance the agent tasks pane in the frontend UI to improve user experience by making agent information more readable, intuitive, and engaging. The current interface shows cryptic agent IDs like \\"exec_dir_1\\" but should display meaningful names, organized information, and expanded whimsical naming.\\n\\n## Core Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Features\\n1. **Readable Agent Names**: Replace technical IDs with whimsical names in the agent tasks pane\\n2. **Agent Type Tags**: Display agent type as a visual tag/badge instead of just text\\n3. **Always Show Whimsical Names**: Ensure whimsical names appear prominently in all agent displays\\n4. **Expanded Whimsical Names**: Add more creative, family-friendly adjectives and nouns to the naming system\\n5. **Achievements Leaderboard**: Add a username-based leaderboard to the achievements page\\n6. **Username Achievements**: Create achievements specifically related to creative usernames\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n- Agent tasks pane shows descriptive names instead of technical IDs\\n- Agent types are visually distinct with badge/tag styling\\n- Whimsical names appear consistently across all agent displays\\n- Expanded name pool provides more variety and creativity\\n- Achievements page includes a leaderboard organized by username\\n- New achievements reward creative username choices\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Frontend Components to Modify\\n1. **AgentSummaryPane.jsx** - Currently shows whimsical names but needs to ensure they\'re always prominent\\n2. **AgentStatusPane.jsx** - Shows agent ID as header, needs whimsical name display\\n3. **AchievementsDashboard.jsx** - Add leaderboard section and username-related achievements\\n4. **whimsicalNames.js** - Expand ADJECTIVES and NOUNS arrays significantly\\n\\n### UI/UX Specifications\\n- **Agent Name Display**: Whimsical name as primary identifier, technical ID as secondary/subtitle\\n- **Agent Type Tags**: Use Bootstrap badges or similar styling with color coding\\n- **Leaderboard**: Table format showing username, total points, achievement count\\n- **Username Achievements**: Badges for creative username patterns, wordplay, themes\\n\\n### Data Requirements\\n- Username tracking for leaderboard functionality\\n- Achievement system integration for username-based rewards\\n- Consistent agent naming across all UI components\\n\\n## Implementation Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Modify existing agent display components\\n- Expand whimsical name generation with 50+ new adjectives/nouns\\n- Add leaderboard section to achievements page\\n- Create 5-10 new username-related achievements\\n- Ensure consistent whimsical name display across all agent interfaces\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Backend API changes (unless required for leaderboard data)\\n- User management system modifications\\n- Achievement calculation algorithm changes\\n- Performance optimizations beyond standard practices\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Current whimsical name generation system is working correctly\\n- Achievement system backend can support username-based achievements\\n- Bootstrap styling is available for badge/tag components\\n- Username data is accessible for leaderboard functionality\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must maintain backward compatibility with existing agent tracking\\n- Should not impact agent performance or execution\\n- Leaderboard should load efficiently with existing data structures\\n- New achievements should integrate with current achievement framework\\n\\n## User Experience Goals\\n- More engaging and memorable agent identification\\n- Visual clarity in agent type differentiation  \\n- Gamification enhancement through username achievements\\n- Social engagement through leaderboard competition\\n- Family-friendly and inclusive naming conventions"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01J49HtGD5d6L3DznFa7tN3G', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01J49HtGD5d6L3DznFa7tN3G', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "main", "changes": {"staged": [{"file": "ogs/ensemble-backend.log.1", "status": "M"}], "unstaged": [{"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.2", "status": "M"}, {"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.3", "status": "M"}, {"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.4", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m2.md", "status": "M"}], "untracked": ["logs/ensemble-backend.log.5"]}, "has_changes": true, "clean": false, "ahead": 8, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "7117f0e3c91789f63c6709b1362d3a66b27ab5cf", "message": "Complete milestone 1 planning and implementation: theme infrastructure and core switcher component", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "4 minutes ago"}, "stash_count": 0}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01N6hDpBthce8kg9caFUEpoz', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Agent Tasks UI Enhancement - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nEnhance the agent tasks pane in the frontend UI to improve user experience by making agent information more readable, intuitive, and engaging. Transform technical agent IDs into whimsical names with visual tags and add leaderboard functionality.\n\n## Milestone 1: Agent Name Enhancement & Visual Tags\n**Duration**: 2-3 days  \n**Priority**: High  \n\n### Objectives\n- Replace technical agent IDs with prominent whimsical names in all agent displays\n- Implement visual agent type tags/badges\n- Expand whimsical name generation system\n\n### Deliverables\n- Modified AgentSummaryPane.jsx with enhanced name display\n- Updated AgentStatusPane.jsx to show whimsical names as primary identifier\n- Enhanced whimsicalNames.js with 50+ new adjectives and nouns\n- Implemented agent type badges with Bootstrap styling\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Whimsical names appear prominently in agent tasks pane\n- Technical IDs shown as secondary/subtitle information\n- Agent types displayed as colored badges/tags\n- Expanded name pool provides more variety\n- All agent displays consistently use whimsical names\n\n### Dependencies\n- Current whimsical name generation system\n- Bootstrap styling framework\n- Existing agent tracking infrastructure\n\n## Milestone 2: Achievements Leaderboard & Username Features\n**Duration**: 2-3 days  \n**Priority**: Medium  \n\n### Objectives\n- Add username-based leaderboard to achievements page\n- Create new username-related achievements\n- Integrate leaderboard with existing achievement system\n\n### Deliverables\n- Enhanced AchievementsDashboard.jsx with leaderboard section\n- New username-based achievements (5-10 achievements)\n- Leaderboard table showing username, points, achievement count\n- Username achievement badge system\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Leaderboard displays user rankings by total points\n- Username achievements reward creative naming patterns\n- Leaderboard loads efficiently with current data structures\n- New achievements integrate seamlessly with existing framework\n\n### Dependencies\n- Completion of Milestone 1\n- Username data accessibility\n- Existing achievement calculation system\n- Achievement system backend compatibility\n\n## Risk Assessment & Mitigation\n\n### Technical Risks\n- **Risk**: Agent name changes could break existing functionality\n- **Mitigation**: Maintain backward compatibility with technical IDs as fallback\n\n- **Risk**: Leaderboard performance issues with large datasets\n- **Mitigation**: Implement efficient data loading and pagination if needed\n\n- **Risk**: Username data unavailable for leaderboard\n- **Mitigation**: Verify data accessibility early; implement mock data if necessary\n\n### Timeline Risks\n- **Risk**: Component modifications more complex than expected\n- **Mitigation**: Start with AgentSummaryPane as proof of concept\n\n## Success Metrics\n- Agent tasks pane shows descriptive whimsical names as primary identifiers\n- Visual agent type differentiation through badges\n- Functional leaderboard with accurate user rankings\n- Enhanced user engagement through gamification features\n- Zero regression in existing agent functionality\n\n## Communication Plan\n- Daily progress updates on milestone completion\n- Early escalation if username data access issues discovered\n- Demo of enhanced UI components upon milestone completion'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01N6hDpBthce8kg9caFUEpoz', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_013219.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_013219.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 91.3%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.9\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n- I effectively managed the complete project lifecycle from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Successfully executed all phases sequentially: milestone planning, architecture des...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
