{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 01:33:26", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-3006a4d4-310e-461c-80c8-c3b216af4c93', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "Agent Tasks UI Enhancement"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NKuestxLF8gDDy8k5LzCyw', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NKuestxLF8gDDy8k5LzCyw', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Agent Tasks UI Enhancement - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nEnhance the agent tasks pane in the frontend UI to improve user experience by making agent information more readable, intuitive, and engaging. The current interface shows cryptic agent IDs like \\"exec_dir_1\\" but should display meaningful names, organized information, and expanded whimsical naming.\\n\\n## Core Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Features\\n1. **Readable Agent Names**: Replace technical IDs with whimsical names in the agent tasks pane\\n2. **Agent Type Tags**: Display agent type as a visual tag/badge instead of just text\\n3. **Always Show Whimsical Names**: Ensure whimsical names appear prominently in all agent displays\\n4. **Expanded Whimsical Names**: Add more creative, family-friendly adjectives and nouns to the naming system\\n5. **Achievements Leaderboard**: Add a username-based leaderboard to the achievements page\\n6. **Username Achievements**: Create achievements specifically related to creative usernames\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n- Agent tasks pane shows descriptive names instead of technical IDs\\n- Agent types are visually distinct with badge/tag styling\\n- Whimsical names appear consistently across all agent displays\\n- Expanded name pool provides more variety and creativity\\n- Achievements page includes a leaderboard organized by username\\n- New achievements reward creative username choices\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Frontend Components to Modify\\n1. **AgentSummaryPane.jsx** - Currently shows whimsical names but needs to ensure they\'re always prominent\\n2. **AgentStatusPane.jsx** - Shows agent ID as header, needs whimsical name display\\n3. **AchievementsDashboard.jsx** - Add leaderboard section and username-related achievements\\n4. **whimsicalNames.js** - Expand ADJECTIVES and NOUNS arrays significantly\\n\\n### UI/UX Specifications\\n- **Agent Name Display**: Whimsical name as primary identifier, technical ID as secondary/subtitle\\n- **Agent Type Tags**: Use Bootstrap badges or similar styling with color coding\\n- **Leaderboard**: Table format showing username, total points, achievement count\\n- **Username Achievements**: Badges for creative username patterns, wordplay, themes\\n\\n### Data Requirements\\n- Username tracking for leaderboard functionality\\n- Achievement system integration for username-based rewards\\n- Consistent agent naming across all UI components\\n\\n## Implementation Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Modify existing agent display components\\n- Expand whimsical name generation with 50+ new adjectives/nouns\\n- Add leaderboard section to achievements page\\n- Create 5-10 new username-related achievements\\n- Ensure consistent whimsical name display across all agent interfaces\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Backend API changes (unless required for leaderboard data)\\n- User management system modifications\\n- Achievement calculation algorithm changes\\n- Performance optimizations beyond standard practices\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Current whimsical name generation system is working correctly\\n- Achievement system backend can support username-based achievements\\n- Bootstrap styling is available for badge/tag components\\n- Username data is accessible for leaderboard functionality\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must maintain backward compatibility with existing agent tracking\\n- Should not impact agent performance or execution\\n- Leaderboard should load efficiently with existing data structures\\n- New achievements should integrate with current achievement framework\\n\\n## User Experience Goals\\n- More engaging and memorable agent identification\\n- Visual clarity in agent type differentiation  \\n- Gamification enhancement through username achievements\\n- Social engagement through leaderboard competition\\n- Family-friendly and inclusive naming conventions"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01CAA4J88gNGRyKjqrxGvYTB', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Agent Tasks UI Enhancement - Architecture Proposal\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\n### High-Level Design\nThis enhancement follows a **Component-Based Architecture** pattern, focusing on modular UI components that can be independently updated while maintaining system cohesion. The architecture leverages React\'s component hierarchy to implement cascading data flow for agent information display.\n\n**Architecture Pattern**: Presentational/Container Component Pattern\n- Container components handle data fetching and state management\n- Presentational components focus purely on UI rendering\n- Shared services provide consistent data transformation\n\n**Rationale**: This approach minimizes risk by working within the existing React architecture while enabling focused enhancements to specific UI components without system-wide changes.\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n### Frontend Framework & Libraries\n- **React.js** (existing) - Component-based UI framework\n  - *Why*: Already established in the codebase, proven for UI enhancements\n  - *Alternatives considered*: Vue.js (rejected - would require complete rewrite)\n\n- **Bootstrap** (existing) - CSS framework for badges and styling  \n  - *Why*: Provides ready-made badge components, consistent with existing design\n  - *Alternatives considered*: Tailwind CSS (rejected - would require design system changes)\n\n- **JavaScript ES6+** - For enhanced name generation and data manipulation\n  - *Why*: Native browser support, no additional dependencies\n  - *Alternatives considered*: TypeScript (rejected - not currently used in project)\n\n### State Management\n- **React Context API** - For agent display preferences and naming state\n  - *Why*: Lightweight solution for sharing agent naming data across components\n  - *Alternatives considered*: Redux (rejected - overkill for this enhancement scope)\n\n### Data Processing\n- **Native JavaScript Arrays/Objects** - For whimsical name generation and leaderboard sorting\n  - *Why*: Simple, performant, no external dependencies\n  - *Alternatives considered*: Lodash (rejected - unnecessary for this scope)\n\n## System Components\n\n### Core Components Architecture\n\n```\nAgentNamingService (New)\n├── WhimsicalNameGenerator (Enhanced)\n├── AgentTypeTagRenderer (New)\n└── AgentDisplayFormatter (New)\n\nUI Components (Modified)\n├── AgentSummaryPane.jsx (Enhanced)\n├── AgentStatusPane.jsx (Enhanced)  \n├── AchievementsDashboard.jsx (Enhanced)\n└── UsernameLeaderboard.jsx (New)\n\nData Layer\n├── whimsicalNames.js (Expanded)\n├── achievementsData.js (Enhanced)\n└── leaderboardService.js (New)\n```\n\n### Component Responsibilities\n\n**AgentNamingService** (New Service)\n- Centralized agent name generation and caching\n- Consistent name-to-ID mapping across components\n- Agent type badge styling logic\n\n**WhimsicalNameGenerator** (Enhanced)\n- Expanded adjective/noun pools (50+ each)\n- Deterministic name generation (same ID = same name)\n- Family-friendly content filtering\n\n**AgentDisplayFormatter** (New Utility)\n- Standardized agent information formatting\n- Primary/secondary text hierarchy management\n- Type badge integration\n\n**AgentSummaryPane.jsx** (Enhanced)\n- Prominent whimsical name display\n- Agent type badges\n- Consistent styling with other panes\n\n**AgentStatusPane.jsx** (Enhanced)  \n- Whimsical name as header\n- Technical ID as subtitle\n- Agent type badge integration\n\n**UsernameLeaderboard.jsx** (New Component)\n- Username-based ranking display\n- Achievement count integration\n- Responsive table layout\n\n### Data Flow\n\n```\nAgent Data → AgentNamingService → WhimsicalNameGenerator\n     ↓              ↓                      ↓\nDisplay Components ← AgentDisplayFormatter ← Generated Names\n     ↓\nUser Interface (Consistent agent naming across all views)\n\nUsername Data → LeaderboardService → UsernameLeaderboard\n     ↓               ↓                    ↓\nAchievement System ← Achievement Tracker ← Username Achievements\n```\n\n## File/Directory Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── components/\n│   ├── agent/\n│   │   ├── AgentSummaryPane.jsx (modified)\n│   │   ├── AgentStatusPane.jsx (modified)\n│   │   └── AgentTypeTag.jsx (new)\n│   ├── achievements/\n│   │   ├── AchievementsDashboard.jsx (modified)\n│   │   ├── UsernameLeaderboard.jsx (new)\n│   │   └── UsernameAchievements.jsx (new)\n├── services/\n│   ├── AgentNamingService.js (new)\n│   ├── AgentDisplayFormatter.js (new)\n│   └── LeaderboardService.js (new)\n├── utils/\n│   ├── whimsicalNames.js (enhanced)\n│   └── achievementHelpers.js (enhanced)\n├── styles/\n│   ├── agentTags.css (new)\n│   └── leaderboard.css (new)\n```\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Agent Display Data Structure\n```javascript\n{\n  agentId: "exec_dir_1",\n  whimsicalName: "Brilliant Falcon",\n  agentType: "executor",\n  status: "running",\n  displayName: {\n    primary: "Brilliant Falcon",\n    secondary: "exec_dir_1",\n    badge: {\n      text: "Executor", \n      color: "primary"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Expanded Whimsical Names Structure\n```javascript\n{\n  ADJECTIVES: [\n    // Existing + 50 new entries\n    "Brilliant", "Swift", "Clever", "Mighty", "Gentle",\n    "Daring", "Cheerful", "Wise", "Brave", "Curious",\n    // ... expanded list\n  ],\n  NOUNS: [\n    // Existing + 50 new entries  \n    "Falcon", "Phoenix", "Dragon", "Eagle", "Wolf",\n    "Butterfly", "Dolphin", "Tiger", "Owl", "Bear",\n    // ... expanded list\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Leaderboard Data Structure\n```javascript\n{\n  username: "string",\n  totalPoints: "number", \n  achievementCount: "number",\n  usernameAchievements: ["achievement_id"],\n  rank: "number"\n}\n```\n\n## API Design\n\n### Internal Service APIs\n\n**AgentNamingService API**\n```javascript\n// Get consistent whimsical name for agent\ngetWhimsicalName(agentId): string\n\n// Get formatted display data for agent\ngetAgentDisplayData(agentId, agentType): AgentDisplayData\n\n// Get styled badge configuration for agent type\ngetAgentTypeBadge(agentType): BadgeConfig\n```\n\n**LeaderboardService API**\n```javascript\n// Get sorted leaderboard data\ngetLeaderboard(): Promise<LeaderboardEntry[]>\n\n// Check for new username achievements\ncheckUsernameAchievements(username): AchievementResult[]\n```\n\n### No external API changes required - all enhancements work with existing data structures.\n\n## Deployment Strategy\n\n### Development Approach\n1. **Feature Branch Development** - Create feature branch for UI enhancements\n2. **Component-by-Component Implementation** - Implement and test each component individually\n3. **Integration Testing** - Verify consistent naming across all components\n4. **Staging Deployment** - Test in staging environment before production\n\n### Environment Configuration\n- **Development**: Hot reloading for rapid component iteration\n- **Staging**: Full feature testing with production-like data\n- **Production**: Standard React build process, no additional configuration needed\n\n### CI/CD Integration\n- **Unit Tests**: Jest tests for naming service and utility functions\n- **Component Tests**: React Testing Library for UI component validation\n- **Integration Tests**: End-to-end testing for consistent agent display\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Testing Approach\n**WhimsicalNameGenerator Tests**\n```javascript\n// Test deterministic name generation\nexpect(generateName("exec_dir_1")).toBe("Brilliant Falcon")\nexpect(generateName("exec_dir_1")).toBe("Brilliant Falcon") // Same result\n\n// Test expanded vocabulary usage\nexpect(getUniqueNamesCount()).toBeGreaterThan(2500) // 50x50 combinations\n```\n\n**AgentDisplayFormatter Tests**\n```javascript\n// Test proper formatting structure\nconst formatted = formatAgentDisplay("exec_dir_1", "executor")\nexpect(formatted.primary).toBe("Brilliant Falcon")\nexpect(formatted.secondary).toBe("exec_dir_1")\nexpect(formatted.badge.text).toBe("Executor")\n```\n\n### Integration Testing Approach\n**Cross-Component Consistency Tests**\n- Verify same agent shows identical name across AgentSummaryPane and AgentStatusPane\n- Test that agent type badges render consistently\n- Validate leaderboard integration with achievements system\n\n**User Experience Tests**\n- Test whimsical names appear prominently in all views\n- Verify agent type tags are visually distinct\n- Validate leaderboard sorting and display functionality\n\n### Requirements Verification\n- ✅ Agent tasks pane shows descriptive names instead of technical IDs\n- ✅ Agent types are visually distinct with badge/tag styling  \n- ✅ Whimsical names appear consistently across all agent displays\n- ✅ Expanded name pool provides more variety and creativity\n- ✅ Achievements page includes username-based leaderboard\n- ✅ New achievements reward creative username choices\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### Alternative 1: Backend Name Generation\n**Approach**: Generate whimsical names in backend, store in database\n**Pros**: Consistent across sessions, no frontend computation\n**Cons**: Requires backend changes (out of scope), adds database complexity\n**Decision**: Rejected - violates project constraints\n\n### Alternative 2: Redux State Management  \n**Approach**: Use Redux for agent naming state management\n**Pros**: Centralized state management, time-travel debugging\n**Cons**: Overkill for simple name mapping, adds complexity and bundle size\n**Decision**: Rejected - React Context sufficient for this scope\n\n### Alternative 3: CSS-Only Agent Type Styling\n**Approach**: Use pure CSS classes instead of Bootstrap badges\n**Pros**: Custom styling, reduced dependency on Bootstrap\n**Cons**: More development time, inconsistent with existing design patterns\n**Decision**: Rejected - Bootstrap badges provide consistency and speed\n\n### Alternative 4: Real-time Leaderboard Updates\n**Approach**: WebSocket-based live leaderboard updates\n**Pros**: Real-time user engagement, dynamic competition\n**Cons**: Requires backend infrastructure changes, adds complexity\n**Decision**: Rejected - static leaderboard meets requirements with lower risk\n\n## Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Risk 1: Name Generation Performance\n**Risk**: Generating whimsical names on-demand could cause UI lag\n**Mitigation**: Implement caching in AgentNamingService, generate names once per agent ID\n**Monitoring**: Performance profiling during testing phase\n\n### Risk 2: Name Consistency Across Sessions\n**Risk**: Users might see different names for same agent across browser sessions\n**Mitigation**: Use deterministic algorithm based on agent ID hash\n**Fallback**: Local storage caching for session persistence\n\n### Risk 3: Bootstrap Badge Styling Conflicts\n**Risk**: Agent type badges might conflict with existing Bootstrap usage\n**Mitigation**: Use scoped CSS classes, test against existing UI components\n**Fallback**: Custom CSS badge implementation if conflicts arise\n\n### Risk 4: Leaderboard Performance with Large Datasets  \n**Risk**: Username leaderboard could slow down with many users\n**Mitigation**: Implement client-side pagination, limit initial load to top 100\n**Monitoring**: Performance testing with simulated large datasets\n\n### Risk 5: Achievement Integration Complexity\n**Risk**: Username achievements might conflict with existing achievement system\n**Mitigation**: Extend existing patterns, thorough integration testing\n**Fallback**: Implement as separate achievement category\n\n## Open Questions\n\n### User Preference Questions\n1. **Agent Type Badge Colors**: Should each agent type have distinct colors, or use semantic colors (success/info/warning)?\n   - *Recommendation*: Distinct colors for better visual differentiation\n\n2. **Leaderboard Display Count**: How many users should appear on initial leaderboard load?\n   - *Recommendation*: Top 50 users with "Show More" option\n\n3. **Username Achievement Criteria**: What constitutes a "creative" username for achievements?\n   - *Recommendation*: Wordplay detection, themed usernames, character count variations\n\n### Technical Decision Points\n4. **Name Caching Strategy**: Should whimsical names persist across browser sessions?\n   - *Recommendation*: Yes, using localStorage for better user experience\n\n5. **Agent Type Badge Placement**: Should badges appear before or after agent names?\n   - *Recommendation*: After names to maintain name prominence\n\n## Implementation Priority\n\n### Phase 1 (Core Functionality)\n1. Expand whimsicalNames.js with additional adjectives/nouns\n2. Create AgentNamingService for consistent name generation\n3. Update AgentStatusPane.jsx with whimsical name headers\n4. Implement AgentTypeTag component with Bootstrap badges\n\n### Phase 2 (Enhanced Display)  \n1. Update AgentSummaryPane.jsx for consistent naming\n2. Create AgentDisplayFormatter utility\n3. Add agent type badge integration across all components\n4. Comprehensive cross-component testing\n\n### Phase 3 (Achievements & Leaderboard)\n1. Create UsernameLeaderboard component\n2. Implement LeaderboardService\n3. Design and implement username-based achievements  \n4. Integrate leaderboard into AchievementsDashboard\n\n### Phase 4 (Polish & Testing)\n1. Performance optimization and caching\n2. Comprehensive testing suite\n3. UI/UX refinements based on user feedback\n4. Documentation and deployment preparation\n\nThis architecture provides a solid foundation for enhanced agent UI display while maintaining system stability and meeting all specified requirements.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CAA4J88gNGRyKjqrxGvYTB', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260115_013326.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260115_013326.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.6\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully analyzed the theme switcher requirements and designed a performance-focused architecture that leverages CSS Custom Properties for instant theme switching. The proposal addresses all fun...\n- I successfully analyzed the UI readability requirements and designed a focused, practical architecture that addresses the contrast issues without over-engineering. The proposal correctly identifies th...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status