{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 01:35:23", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-50669148-b90c-402f-8d41-cad6426456ca', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Token Tracking Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UU29xGNQUawYjCeFFw36gt', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UU29xGNQUawYjCeFFw36gt', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Token Tracking Implementation - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name**: Token Tracking Implementation  \\n**Objective**: Implement comprehensive token tracking for all API calls in the ensemble agent system to enable accurate cost calculation and performance monitoring.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nThe ensemble agent system currently passes `tokens_used=None` to the activity tracker for all API calls. This prevents accurate cost calculation, performance analysis, and resource optimization. Token usage data from the Anthropic API responses needs to be extracted, stored, and made available through existing endpoints.\\n\\n## Vision Statement\\n\\nEnable complete visibility into token usage across the ensemble agent system by capturing, storing, and exposing real token consumption data from every API call, facilitating accurate cost tracking, performance optimization, and resource management.\\n\\n## Core Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Token Extraction from API Responses\\n- **Requirement**: Extract actual token counts from Anthropic API responses in `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\\n- **Details**: \\n  - Capture `input_tokens` and `output_tokens` from `response.usage`\\n  - Maintain running totals for each agent execution\\n  - Log token usage per iteration for debugging\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  - Every API call records actual token usage instead of `None`\\n  - Token counts are accumulated across iterations\\n  - Debug logging shows per-iteration token usage\\n\\n### 2. ActivityTracker Token Storage\\n- **Requirement**: Update `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` to store comprehensive token data\\n- **Details**:\\n  - Add `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `total_tokens` parameters to relevant methods\\n  - Store token data in agent state and hierarchy records\\n  - Maintain token tracking in activity records\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  - `record_agent_completed()` accepts and stores token parameters\\n  - Agent states include token usage data\\n  - Activity records contain token information\\n\\n### 3. Cost Calculation Enhancement\\n- **Requirement**: Integrate real token data into cost calculations\\n- **Details**:\\n  - Use actual token counts instead of estimates\\n  - Support per-agent and aggregate cost calculations\\n  - Maintain existing cost calculation interfaces\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  - Cost estimates use real token data\\n  - Agent completion records include accurate costs\\n  - Existing cost calculation functionality preserved\\n\\n### 4. API Endpoint Exposure\\n- **Requirement**: Expose token metrics through existing API endpoints in `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\\n- **Details**:\\n  - Include token data in agent state responses\\n  - Add token aggregation to request timeline data\\n  - Maintain backward compatibility with existing endpoints\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  - `/api/agents/state` endpoint returns token usage data\\n  - `/api/requests/{request_id}/timeline` includes token metrics\\n  - Existing API contracts unchanged\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Performance Requirements\\n- Token extraction adds minimal latency to API calls\\n- Token data storage does not significantly impact memory usage\\n- API responses include token data without performance degradation\\n\\n### Data Requirements\\n- Token counts stored as integers\\n- Support for input, output, and total token tracking\\n- Historical token data preserved across agent executions\\n\\n### Integration Requirements\\n- No breaking changes to existing interfaces\\n- Backward compatibility with current cost calculation system\\n- Seamless integration with existing activity tracking\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n### Scope Limitations\\n- **Backend-only implementation** - no UI modifications required\\n- Focus on Anthropic API token extraction only\\n- No changes to existing agent definitions or tool interfaces\\n\\n### Technical Constraints\\n- Must use existing ActivityTracker infrastructure\\n- Cannot modify agent execution flow significantly\\n- Must maintain existing error handling and resilience patterns\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n\\n1. **`src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`**\\n   - Extract token usage from `response.usage` \\n   - Pass real token data to activity tracker\\n   - Update cost calculation calls\\n\\n2. **`src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`**\\n   - Add token parameters to `record_agent_completed()` method\\n   - Store token data in agent states and hierarchy\\n   - Include token information in activity records\\n\\n3. **`src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`** (if needed)\\n   - Ensure token data flows through API endpoints\\n   - Add token aggregation to timeline responses\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n### Primary Success Criteria\\n1. **Token Extraction**: Every API call records actual token usage\\n2. **Data Storage**: Token counts visible in agent state API responses\\n3. **Cost Accuracy**: Cost calculations use real token data instead of estimates\\n4. **API Visibility**: Token metrics available through existing endpoints\\n\\n### Testing Criteria\\n1. **Unit Tests**: Verify token extraction from mock API responses\\n2. **Integration Tests**: Confirm token data flows through activity tracker\\n3. **API Tests**: Validate token data appears in endpoint responses\\n4. **Cost Tests**: Verify cost calculations use real token data\\n\\n### Performance Criteria\\n- Token extraction adds <1ms latency per API call\\n- Token storage increases memory usage by <5%\\n- API response times remain within current SLAs\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n### Phase 1: Runtime Token Extraction\\n- Modify `AgentRuntime.execute()` to extract tokens from `response.usage`\\n- Update token accumulation logic\\n- Add debug logging for token usage\\n\\n### Phase 2: ActivityTracker Integration  \\n- Update `record_agent_completed()` method signature\\n- Store token data in agent states and hierarchy\\n- Ensure backward compatibility\\n\\n### Phase 3: Cost Calculation Update\\n- Integrate real token data into cost calculations\\n- Update cost estimation logic\\n- Verify cost accuracy improvements\\n\\n### Phase 4: API Endpoint Integration\\n- Ensure token data flows through existing endpoints\\n- Add token aggregation where appropriate\\n- Validate API response structures\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Anthropic API Structure**: Response objects consistently include `usage.input_tokens` and `usage.output_tokens`\\n2. **Existing Infrastructure**: Current ActivityTracker and cost calculation systems can accommodate token data\\n3. **Performance Impact**: Token extraction overhead is negligible compared to API call latency\\n4. **Backward Compatibility**: Existing systems can handle additional token parameters gracefully\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- UI modifications or new frontend components\\n- Token tracking for non-Anthropic API calls\\n- Historical data migration for existing records\\n- Token usage alerts or monitoring systems\\n- Token-based rate limiting or quota management\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- Anthropic Python SDK with usage tracking support\\n- Existing ActivityTracker infrastructure\\n- Current cost calculation system\\n- FastAPI backend endpoints\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n\\n### Technical Risks\\n- **API Response Structure Changes**: Monitor Anthropic API documentation for changes\\n- **Performance Degradation**: Implement efficient token extraction and storage\\n- **Memory Usage**: Use appropriate data types and cleanup strategies\\n\\n### Implementation Risks\\n- **Breaking Changes**: Maintain backward compatibility throughout implementation\\n- **Data Integrity**: Ensure token data consistency across all tracking points\\n- **Error Handling**: Graceful degradation when token data unavailable"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RnB8C8DeHt9Qq17UmDYzC7', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Token Tracking Implementation - Milestone Plan\n\n## Milestone 1: Runtime Token Extraction and Basic Integration\n### Objectives\n- Extract token usage from Anthropic API responses\n- Update `runtime.py` to capture token data\n- Add initial logging and debug support\n\n### Deliverables\n- Modified `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\n- Updated token extraction logic\n- Debug logging for token usage\n- Initial unit tests for token extraction\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Token counts captured for each API call\n- Debug logs show input, output, and total tokens\n- Unit tests verify token extraction accuracy\n\n## Milestone 2: ActivityTracker and Cost Calculation Integration\n### Objectives\n- Update ActivityTracker to store token data\n- Integrate token information into agent states\n- Modify cost calculation logic\n\n### Deliverables\n- Modified `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\n- Updated agent state and hierarchy tracking\n- Revised cost calculation methods\n- Integration tests for token data storage\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Token data stored in agent states\n- Cost calculations use real token data\n- Backward compatibility maintained\n\n## Milestone 3: API Endpoint and Final Integration\n### Objectives\n- Expose token metrics through existing endpoints\n- Perform comprehensive integration testing\n- Validate performance and minimal overhead\n\n### Deliverables\n- Updated `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\n- Complete API response token integration\n- Performance benchmark tests\n- Final system validation\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Token data visible in API responses\n- API performance within original SLAs\n- All system components functioning correctly\n\n## Dependencies Between Milestones\n1. Milestone 1 must complete before Milestone 2\n2. Milestone 2 must complete before Milestone 3\n3. Final validation requires successful completion of all milestones'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RnB8C8DeHt9Qq17UmDYzC7', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_013523.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_013523.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones"