{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 01:35:29", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-f9dd3a02-814b-46e6-858d-fdfa2f01d61c', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014a8EAypLP5K7mQ29mRbiRH', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014a8EAypLP5K7mQ29mRbiRH', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Token Tracking Implementation - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name**: Token Tracking Implementation  \\n**Objective**: Implement comprehensive token tracking for all API calls in the ensemble agent system to enable accurate cost calculation and performance monitoring.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nThe ensemble agent system currently passes `tokens_used=None` to the activity tracker for all API calls. This prevents accurate cost calculation, performance analysis, and resource optimization. Token usage data from the Anthropic API responses needs to be extracted, stored, and made available through existing endpoints.\\n\\n## Vision Statement\\n\\nEnable complete visibility into token usage across the ensemble agent system by capturing, storing, and exposing real token consumption data from every API call, facilitating accurate cost tracking, performance optimization, and resource management.\\n\\n## Core Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Token Extraction from API Responses\\n- **Requirement**: Extract actual token counts from Anthropic API responses in `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\\n- **Details**: \\n  - Capture `input_tokens` and `output_tokens` from `response.usage`\\n  - Maintain running totals for each agent execution\\n  - Log token usage per iteration for debugging\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  - Every API call records actual token usage instead of `None`\\n  - Token counts are accumulated across iterations\\n  - Debug logging shows per-iteration token usage\\n\\n### 2. ActivityTracker Token Storage\\n- **Requirement**: Update `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` to store comprehensive token data\\n- **Details**:\\n  - Add `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `total_tokens` parameters to relevant methods\\n  - Store token data in agent state and hierarchy records\\n  - Maintain token tracking in activity records\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  - `record_agent_completed()` accepts and stores token parameters\\n  - Agent states include token usage data\\n  - Activity records contain token information\\n\\n### 3. Cost Calculation Enhancement\\n- **Requirement**: Integrate real token data into cost calculations\\n- **Details**:\\n  - Use actual token counts instead of estimates\\n  - Support per-agent and aggregate cost calculations\\n  - Maintain existing cost calculation interfaces\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  - Cost estimates use real token data\\n  - Agent completion records include accurate costs\\n  - Existing cost calculation functionality preserved\\n\\n### 4. API Endpoint Exposure\\n- **Requirement**: Expose token metrics through existing API endpoints in `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\\n- **Details**:\\n  - Include token data in agent state responses\\n  - Add token aggregation to request timeline data\\n  - Maintain backward compatibility with existing endpoints\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  - `/api/agents/state` endpoint returns token usage data\\n  - `/api/requests/{request_id}/timeline` includes token metrics\\n  - Existing API contracts unchanged\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Performance Requirements\\n- Token extraction adds minimal latency to API calls\\n- Token data storage does not significantly impact memory usage\\n- API responses include token data without performance degradation\\n\\n### Data Requirements\\n- Token counts stored as integers\\n- Support for input, output, and total token tracking\\n- Historical token data preserved across agent executions\\n\\n### Integration Requirements\\n- No breaking changes to existing interfaces\\n- Backward compatibility with current cost calculation system\\n- Seamless integration with existing activity tracking\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n### Scope Limitations\\n- **Backend-only implementation** - no UI modifications required\\n- Focus on Anthropic API token extraction only\\n- No changes to existing agent definitions or tool interfaces\\n\\n### Technical Constraints\\n- Must use existing ActivityTracker infrastructure\\n- Cannot modify agent execution flow significantly\\n- Must maintain existing error handling and resilience patterns\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n\\n1. **`src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`**\\n   - Extract token usage from `response.usage` \\n   - Pass real token data to activity tracker\\n   - Update cost calculation calls\\n\\n2. **`src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`**\\n   - Add token parameters to `record_agent_completed()` method\\n   - Store token data in agent states and hierarchy\\n   - Include token information in activity records\\n\\n3. **`src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`** (if needed)\\n   - Ensure token data flows through API endpoints\\n   - Add token aggregation to timeline responses\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n### Primary Success Criteria\\n1. **Token Extraction**: Every API call records actual token usage\\n2. **Data Storage**: Token counts visible in agent state API responses\\n3. **Cost Accuracy**: Cost calculations use real token data instead of estimates\\n4. **API Visibility**: Token metrics available through existing endpoints\\n\\n### Testing Criteria\\n1. **Unit Tests**: Verify token extraction from mock API responses\\n2. **Integration Tests**: Confirm token data flows through activity tracker\\n3. **API Tests**: Validate token data appears in endpoint responses\\n4. **Cost Tests**: Verify cost calculations use real token data\\n\\n### Performance Criteria\\n- Token extraction adds <1ms latency per API call\\n- Token storage increases memory usage by <5%\\n- API response times remain within current SLAs\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n### Phase 1: Runtime Token Extraction\\n- Modify `AgentRuntime.execute()` to extract tokens from `response.usage`\\n- Update token accumulation logic\\n- Add debug logging for token usage\\n\\n### Phase 2: ActivityTracker Integration  \\n- Update `record_agent_completed()` method signature\\n- Store token data in agent states and hierarchy\\n- Ensure backward compatibility\\n\\n### Phase 3: Cost Calculation Update\\n- Integrate real token data into cost calculations\\n- Update cost estimation logic\\n- Verify cost accuracy improvements\\n\\n### Phase 4: API Endpoint Integration\\n- Ensure token data flows through existing endpoints\\n- Add token aggregation where appropriate\\n- Validate API response structures\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Anthropic API Structure**: Response objects consistently include `usage.input_tokens` and `usage.output_tokens`\\n2. **Existing Infrastructure**: Current ActivityTracker and cost calculation systems can accommodate token data\\n3. **Performance Impact**: Token extraction overhead is negligible compared to API call latency\\n4. **Backward Compatibility**: Existing systems can handle additional token parameters gracefully\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- UI modifications or new frontend components\\n- Token tracking for non-Anthropic API calls\\n- Historical data migration for existing records\\n- Token usage alerts or monitoring systems\\n- Token-based rate limiting or quota management\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- Anthropic Python SDK with usage tracking support\\n- Existing ActivityTracker infrastructure\\n- Current cost calculation system\\n- FastAPI backend endpoints\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n\\n### Technical Risks\\n- **API Response Structure Changes**: Monitor Anthropic API documentation for changes\\n- **Performance Degradation**: Implement efficient token extraction and storage\\n- **Memory Usage**: Use appropriate data types and cleanup strategies\\n\\n### Implementation Risks\\n- **Breaking Changes**: Maintain backward compatibility throughout implementation\\n- **Data Integrity**: Ensure token data consistency across all tracking points\\n- **Error Handling**: Graceful degradation when token data unavailable"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud 