dd project grouping and status summary to UI (UI Improvements 2025)", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "28 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "2ac110858b3f8f7b396f61f7f744ca282d360e52", "message": "Add GitHub Bots foundation (Milestone 1)", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "31 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "0bf03ec59f00eab54fc0a75fa35a259d05a6c3a6", "message": "Add TMUX monitoring dashboard scripts (Milestone 1)", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "59 minutes ago"}], "stash_count": 0}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012ZjrEAG3amE1NhzucNvwwz', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012ZjrEAG3amE1NhzucNvwwz', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Activity Feed Selector Fix Requirements\\n\\n## Problem Description\\nThe activity feed dropdown selector in the Ensemble UI does not properly filter activities to show contained agents, error states, or failed agents. Currently only \\"Iteration Started\\" works as expected, while other filter options don\'t function correctly.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Fix the activity feed dropdown selector to properly filter activities\\n2. Enable filtering by agent states (error, failed)\\n3. Ensure all filter options work as expected\\n4. Maintain existing UI design and user experience\\n\\n## Current State Analysis\\n\\n### Issues Identified\\n1. **Hardcoded Filter Options**: The dropdown has limited options that don\'t match all available activity types\\n2. **Simplistic Filter Logic**: Current filtering uses exact string matching against `activity_type` field\\n3. **Missing Agent State Filtering**: Cannot filter by agent states like \\"error\\" or \\"failed\\"\\n4. **Inconsistent Filter Values**: Dropdown options don\'t align with actual activity types in the data\\n\\n### Current Implementation\\n- Located in `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/App.jsx`\\n- Uses `activityFilter` state with hardcoded options\\n- Filter options: \\"all\\", \\"agent_spawned\\", \\"agent_completed\\", \\"tool_use\\", \\"iteration_started\\", \\"error\\"\\n- Filtering logic: `activity.activity_type === activityFilter`\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### R1: Enhanced Filter Options\\n- **Must** support filtering by all available activity types:\\n  - `agent_started`\\n  - `agent_completed` \\n  - `agent_failed`\\n  - `iteration_started`\\n  - `iteration_completed`\\n  - `tool_use_started`\\n  - `tool_use_completed`\\n  - `tool_use_failed`\\n  - `agent_spawned`\\n  - `thinking`\\n  - `message`\\n  - `question`\\n  - `answer`\\n  - `task_update`\\n  - `status_change`\\n\\n### R2: Semantic Filter Categories\\n- **Must** provide high-level filter categories:\\n  - **All Activities**: Show everything\\n  - **Agent Lifecycle**: agent_started, agent_completed, agent_failed, agent_spawned\\n  - **Iterations**: iteration_started, iteration_completed\\n  - **Tool Usage**: tool_use_started, tool_use_completed, tool_use_failed\\n  - **Errors/Failures**: agent_failed, tool_use_failed, messages with error type\\n  - **Communications**: message, question, answer\\n  - **Updates**: task_update, status_change, thinking\\n\\n### R3: Smart Filtering Logic\\n- **Must** implement filtering logic that handles:\\n  - Multiple activity types per filter category\\n  - Message type filtering (for error messages)\\n  - Nested data inspection for error states\\n- **Should** be performant for large activity lists\\n\\n### R4: User Experience\\n- **Must** maintain current UI layout and styling\\n- **Must** show activity count per filter category in dropdown\\n- **Should** preserve user\'s filter selection across app refreshes\\n- **Must** provide clear visual indication of active filter\\n\\n### R5: Error State Handling\\n- **Must** properly identify and filter error activities:\\n  - Activities with `activity_type` containing \\"failed\\"\\n  - Message activities with `data.message_type === \\"error\\"`\\n  - Agent activities with error status in data\\n- **Should** show error details in filtered view\\n\\n## Technical Specifications\\n\\n### Filter Implementation\\n- Replace hardcoded filter options with dynamic categories\\n- Implement category-based filtering function\\n- Add activity type detection utilities\\n- Maintain backward compatibility with existing activity data structure\\n\\n### Data Requirements\\n- No changes to backend API required\\n- No changes to activity data structure required\\n- Enhancement works with existing activity feed data\\n\\n### UI Components\\n- Update dropdown options in App.jsx\\n- Enhance filtering logic in activity filter handler\\n- Maintain existing Badge and UI styling\\n- Add activity count display per filter option\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Functional**: All dropdown filter options work correctly\\n2. **Comprehensive**: Users can filter to see failed/error agents\\n3. **Intuitive**: Filter categories are self-explanatory  \\n4. **Performance**: Filtering is responsive with 200+ activities\\n5. **Visual**: Clear indication of what\'s being filtered and count of results\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- Changes to ActivityFeed component display logic\\n- Modifications to activity data structure or API\\n- Addition of new activity types\\n- Changes to polling or real-time update logic\\n- Search functionality within activities\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n- Must maintain existing UI design language\\n- Must work with current activity data structure\\n- Must not impact application performance\\n- Cannot modify backend API or activity tracking\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- Activity data contains consistent `activity_type` field\\n- Message activities have `data.message_type` field when applicable\\n- Error activities contain identifiable error information\\n- Current activity polling and data fetching logic is adequate"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_013xkF67R7C4oTABdQ1iBHW9', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/App.jsx'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_013xkF67R7C4oTABdQ1iBHW9', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "import React, { useState, useEffect, useRef } from \'react\';\\nimport { Container, Row, Col, Card, Form, Button, Badge, Spinner, Alert, ButtonGroup } from \'react-bootstrap\';\\nimport {\\n  generateSolution,\\n  getApplicationStatus,\\n  getRecentActivities,\\n  getAgentHierarchy,\\n  getAllAgentStates,\\n  getPendingQuestions,\\n  answerQuestion,\\n  getGeneratedFiles\\n} from \'./services/api\';\\nimport ActivityFeed from \'./components/ActivityFeed\';\\nimport AgentHierarchyTree from \'./components/AgentHierarchyTree\';\\nimport StatusSummaryBar from \'./components/StatusSummaryBar\';\\nimport PendingQuestions from \'./components/PendingQuestions\';\\nimport GeneratedFiles from \'./components/GeneratedFiles\';\\nimport MetricsDashboard from \'./components/MetricsDashboard\';\\nimport HorizontalTimelineView from \'./components/HorizontalTimelineView\';\\nimport SelfImprovementDashboard from \'./components/SelfImprovementDashboard\';\\nimport AchievementsDashboard from \'./components/AchievementsDashboard\';\\nimport CostTrackingDashboard from \'./components/CostTrackingDashboard\';\\nimport RecoveryDashboard from \'./components/RecoveryDashboard\';\\n\\nfunction App() {\\n  const [currentView, setCurrentView] = useState(\'main\'); // \'main\', \'metrics\', \'timeline\', \'improve\', \'achievements\', \'costs\', or \'recovery\'\\n  const [problemInput, setProblemInput] = useState(\'\');\\n  const [budgetTier, setBudgetTier] = useState(\'balanced\');\\n  const [isSubmitting, setIsSubmitting] = useState(false);\\n  const [error, setError] = useState(null);\\n\\n  // Activity state\\n  const [activities, setActivities] = useState([]);\\n  const [hierarchy, setHierarchy] = useState({});\\n  const [agentStates, setAgentStates] = useState({});\\n  const [questions, setQuestions] = useState({});\\n  const [generatedFiles, setGeneratedFiles] = useState([]);\\n  const [appStatus, setAppStatus] = useState({ status: \'connecting\', active_agents: 0 });\\n\\n  // Polling configuration\\n  const [pollInterval, setPollInterval] = useState(1000); // 1 second default\\n  const [isPaused, setIsPaused] = useState(false);\\n\\n  // Filter state\\n  const [hideCompleted, setHideCompleted] = useState(false);\\n  const [activityFilter, setActivityFilter] = useState(\'all\'); // all, spawned, completed, tool_use, error\\n  const [agentTypeFilter, setAgentTypeFilter] = useState(\'all\'); // all, leadership, coordinators, developers, testers\\n\\n  // Collapse state\\n  const [sectionsCollapsed, setSectionsCollapsed] = useState({\\n    hierarchy: false,\\n    agents: false,\\n    files: false\\n  });\\n\\n  const pollTimerRef = useRef(null);\\n\\n  // Fetch all activity data\\n  const fetchActivityData = async () => {\\n    if (isPaused) return;\\n\\n    try {\\n      const [activitiesRes, hierarchyRes, statesRes, questionsRes, filesRes, statusRes] = await Promise.all([\\n        getRecentActivities({ limit: 200 }),\\n        getAgentHierarchy(),\\n        getAllAgentStates(),\\n        getPendingQuestions(),\\n        getGeneratedFiles({ limit: 100 }),\\n        getApplicationStatus()\\n      ]);\\n\\n      setActivities(activitiesRes.activities || []);\\n      setHierarchy(hierarchyRes.hierarchy || {});\\n      setAgentStates(statesRes.agent_states || {});\\n      setQuestions(questionsRes.questions || {});\\n      setGeneratedFiles(filesRes.files || []);\\n      setAppStatus(statusRes);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      console.error(\'Failed to fetch activity data:\', err);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  // Set up polling\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    // Initial fetch\\n    fetchActivityData();\\n\\n    // Set up polling\\n    if (pollTimerRef.current) {\\n      clearInterval(pollTimerRef.current);\\n    }\\n\\n    pollTimerRef.current = setInterval(fetchActivityData, pollInterval);\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      if (pollTimerRef.current) {\\n        clearInterval(pollTimerRef.current);\\n      }\\n    };\\n  }, [pollInterval, isPaused]);\\n\\n  const handleSubmit = async (e) => {\\n    e.preventDefault();\\n    setIsSubmitting(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n\\n    try {\\n      const response = await generateSolution(problemInput, budgetTier);\\n      console.log(\'Solution generation started:\', response);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      setError(\'Failed to start solution generation\');\\n      console.error(err);\\n    } finally {\\n      setIsSubmitting(false);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleAnswerQuestion = async (questionId, answer) => {\\n    await answerQuestion(questionId, answer);\\n    // Refresh questions immediately\\n    const questionsRes = await getPendingQuestions();\\n    setQuestions(questionsRes.questions || {});\\n  };\\n\\n  const runningAgents = Object.values(agentStates).filter(s => s.status === \'running\').length;\\n  const completedAgents = Object.values(agentStates).filter(s => s.status === \'completed\').length;\\n  const failedAgents = Object.values(agentStates).filter(s => s.status === \'failed\' || s.status === \'forever_failed\').length;\\n  const foreverFailedAgents = Object.values(agentStates).filter(s => s.status === \'forever_failed\').length;\\n\\n  // Filter agents based on hideCompleted\\n  const filteredAgentStates = Object.entries(agentStates).filter(([_, state]) => {\\n    if (hideCompleted && state.status === \'completed\') return false;\\n    return true;\\n  });\\n\\n  // Filter activities based on activity filter\\n  const filteredActivities = activities.filter(activity => {\\n    if (activityFilter === \'all\') return true;\\n    return activity.activity_type === activityFilter;\\n  });\\n\\n  // Toggle collapse state\\n  const toggleSection = (section) => {\\n    setSectionsCollapsed(prev => ({\\n      ...prev,\\n      [section]: !prev[section]\\n    }));\\n  };\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div style={{ minHeight: \'100vh\', backgroundColor: \'#1a1d29\' }}>\\n      {/* Header */}\\n      <div style={{\\n        backgroundColor: \'#242836\',\\n        borderBottom: \'1px solid #3a3f52\',\\n        padding: \'12px 0\'\\n      }}>\\n        <Container fluid>\\n          <Row>\\n            <Col>\\n              <div style={{ display: \'flex\', alignItems: \'center\', justifyContent: \'space-between\' }}>\\n                <div style={{ display: \'flex\', alignItems: \'center\', gap: \'12px\' }}>\\n                  <h4 style={{ margin: 0, color: \'#e4e6eb\' }}>\\ud83c\\udfad Ensemble AI</h4>\\n                  <Badge bg={appStatus.status === \'running\' ? \'success\' : \'secondary\'}>\\n                    {appStatus.status === \'running\' ? \'Online\' : \'Connecting...\'}\\n                  </Badge>\\n                  <Badge bg=\\"warning\\" text=\\"dark\\">{runningAgents} Running</Badge>\\n                  <Badge bg=\\"success\\">{completedAgents} Completed</Badge>\\n                  {failedAgents > 0 && <Badge bg=\\"danger\\">{failedAgents} Failed</Badge>}\\n                  {foreverFailedAgents > 0 && <Badge bg=\\"dark\\" style={{ border: \'1px solid #dc3545\' }}>\\u2620\\ufe0f {foreverFailedAgents} Terminated</Badge>}\\n                </div>\\n\\n                {/* View Switcher and Poll interval control */}\\n                <div style={{ display: \'flex\', alignItems: \'center\', gap: \'12px\' }}>\\n                  <ButtonGroup size=\\"sm\\">\\n                    <Button\\n                      variant={currentView === \'main\' ? \'primary\' : \'outline-secondary\'}\\n                      onClick={() => setCurrentView(\'main\')}\\n                    >\\n                      \\ud83c\\udfad Activity\\n                    </Button>\\n                    <Button\\n                      variant={currentView === \'timeline\' ? \'primary\' : \'outline-secondary\'}\\n                      onClick={() => setCurrentView(\'timeline\')}\\n                    >\\n                      \\u23f1\\ufe0f Timeline\\n                    </Button>\\n                    <Button\\n                      variant={currentView === \'metrics\' ? \'primary\' : \'outline-secondary\'}\\n                      onClick={() => setCurrentView(\'metrics\')}\\n                    >\\n                      \\ud83d\\udcca Metrics\\n                    </Button>\\n                    <Button\\n                      variant={currentView === \'improve\' ? \'primary\' : \'outline-secondary\'}\\n                      onClick={() => setCurrentView(\'improve\')}\\n                    >\\n                      \\ud83d\\udd04 Improve\\n                    </Button>\\n                    <Button\\n                      variant={currentView === \'achievements\' ? \'primary\' : \'outline-secondary\'}\\n                      onClick={() => setCurrentView(\'achievements\')}\\n                    >\\n                      \\ud83c\\udfc6 Achievements\\n                    </Button>\\n                    <Button\\n                      variant={currentView === \'costs\' ? \'primary\' : \'outline-secondary\'}\\n                      onClick={() => setCurrentView(\'costs\')}\\n                    >\\n                      \\ud83d\\udcb0 Costs\\n                    </Button>\\n                    <Button\\n                      variant={currentView === \'recovery\' ? \'primary\' : \'outline-secondary\'}\\n                      onClick={() => setCurrentView(\'recovery\')}\\n                    >\\n                      \\ud83d\\udd27 Recovery\\n                    </Button>\\n                  </ButtonGroup>\\n\\n                  <span style={{ fontSize: \'12px\', color: \'#9ca3af\' }}>Update Interval:</span>\\n                  <ButtonGroup size=\\"sm\\">\\n                    <Button\\n                      variant={pollInterval === 500 ? \'primary\' : \'outline-secondary\'}\\n                      onClick={() => setPollInterval(500)}\\n                    >\\n                      500ms\\n                    </Button>\\n                    <Button\\n                      variant={pollInterval === 1000 ? \'primary\' : \'outline-secondary\'}\\n                      onClick={() => setPollInterval(1000)}\\n                    >\\n                      1s\\n                    </Button>\\n                    <Button\\n                      variant={pollInterval === 2000 ? \'primary\' : \'outline-secondary\'}\\n                      onClick={() => setPollInterval(2000)}\\n                    >\\n                      2s\\n                    </Button>\\n                  </ButtonGroup>\\n                  <Button\\n                    variant={isPaused ? \'warning\' : \'outline-secondary\'}\\n                    size=\\"sm\\"\\n                    onClick={() => setIsPaused(!isPaused)}\\n                  >\\n                    {isPaused ? \'\\u25b6 Resume\' : \'\\u23f8 Pause\'}\\n                  </Button>\\n                </div>\\n              </div>\\n            </Col>\\n          </Row>\\n        </Container>\\n      </div>\\n\\n      {/* Conditional rendering based on current view */}\\n      {currentView === \'metrics\' ? (\\n        <MetricsDashboard />\\n      ) : currentView === \'timeline\' ? (\\n        <div style={{ height: \'calc(100vh - 80px)\' }}>\\n          <HorizontalTimelineView />\\n        </div>\\n      ) : currentView === \'improve\' ? (\\n        <SelfImprovementDashboard />\\n      ) : currentView === \'achievements\' ? (\\n        <AchievementsDashboard />\\n      ) : currentView === \'costs\' ? (\\n        <CostTrackingDashboard />\\n      ) : currentView === \'recovery\' ? (\\n        <RecoveryDashboard />\\n      ) : (\\n        <>\\n        <Container fluid style={{ padding: \'16px\' }}>\\n        <Row style={{ height: \'calc(100vh - 80px)\' }}>\\n          {/* Left Column - Input & Questions */}\\n          <Col md={3} style={{ height: \'100%\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n            {/* Input Form */}\\n            <Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"light\\" className=\\"mb-3\\">\\n              <Card.Header>\\n                <h6 className=\\"mb-0\\">New Task</h6>\\n              </Card.Header>\\n              <Card.Body>\\n                <Form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>\\n                  <Form.Group className=\\"mb-3\\">\\n                    <Form.Label style={{ fontSize: \'13px\' }}>Problem Description</Form.Label>\\n                    <Form.Control\\n                      as=\\"textarea\\"\\n                      rows={4}\\n                      value={problemInput}\\n                      onChange={(e) => setProblemInput(e.target.value)}\\n                      placeholder=\\"Describe what you want to build...\\"\\n                      style={{\\n                        backgroundColor: \'#1a1d29\',\\n                        color: \'#e4e6eb\',\\n                        border: \'1px solid #3a3f52\',\\n                        fontSize: \'13px\'\\n                      }}\\n                    />\\n                  </Form.Group>\\n\\n                  <Form.Group className=\\"mb-3\\">\\n                    <Form.Label style={{ fontSize: \'13px\' }}>Budget Tier</Form.Label>\\n                    <Form.Select\\n                      value={budgetTier}\\n                      onChange={(e) => setBudgetTier(e.target.value)}\\n                      style={{\\n                        backgroundColor: \'#1a1d29\',\\n                        color: \'#e4e6eb\',\\n                        border: \'1px solid #3a3f52\',\\n                        fontSize: \'13px\'\\n                      }}\\n                    >\\n                      <option value=\\"economical\\">Economical (Haiku)</option>\\n                      <option value=\\"balanced\\">Balanced (Sonnet)</option>\\n                      <option value=\\"full_firepower\\">Full Power (Opus)</option>\\n                    </Form.Select>\\n                  </Form.Group>\\n\\n                  <Button\\n                    variant=\\"primary\\"\\n                    type=\\"submit\\"\\n                    disabled={isSubmitting || !problemInput}\\n                    style={{ width: \'100%\' }}\\n                  >\\n                    {isSubmitting ? (\\n                      <>\\n                        <Spinner animation=\\"border\\" size=\\"sm\\" className=\\"me-2\\" />\\n                        Starting...\\n                      </>\\n                    ) : (\\n                      \'\\ud83d\\ude80 Start Task\'\\n                    )}\\n                  </Button>\\n\\n                  {error && (\\n                    <Alert variant=\\"danger\\" className=\\"mt-3 mb-0\\" style={{ fontSize: \'12px\' }}>\\n                      {error}\\n                    </Alert>\\n                  )}\\n                </Form>\\n              </Card.Body>\\n            </Card>\\n\\n            {/* Pending Questions */}\\n            <PendingQuestions questions={questions} onAnswer={handleAnswerQuestion} />\\n\\n            {/* Agent Hierarchy */}\\n            <Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"light\\">\\n              <Card.Header\\n                style={{ cursor: \'pointer\' }}\\n                onClick={() => toggleSection(\'hierarchy\')}\\n              >\\n                <div style={{ display: \'flex\', justifyContent: \'space-between\', alignItems: \'center\' }}>\\n                  <div>\\n                    <span style={{ marginRight: \'8px\' }}>\\n                      {sectionsCollapsed.hierarchy ? \'\\u25b6\' : \'\\u25bc\'}\\n                    </span>\\n                    <span style={{ fontSize: \'14px\' }}>Agent Hierarchy</span>\\n                    <Badge bg=\\"info\\" className=\\"ms-2\\" style={{ fontSize: \'10px\' }}>\\n                      {Object.keys(hierarchy).length} agents\\n                    </Badge>\\n                  </div>\\n                </div>\\n              </Card.Header>\\n              {!sectionsCollapsed.hierarchy && (\\n                <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'500px\', overflowY: \'auto\', padding: \'12px\' }}>\\n                  <StatusSummaryBar agentStatus={agentStates} />\\n                  <AgentHierarchyTree hierarchy={hierarchy} />\\n                </Card.Body>\\n              )}\\n            </Card>\\n          </Col>\\n\\n          {/* Middle Column - Activity Feed */}\\n          <Col md={5} style={{ height: \'100%\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n            <Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"light\\" style={{ height: \'100%\', display: \'flex\', flexDirection: \'column\' }}>\\n              <Card.Header>\\n                <div style={{ marginBottom: \'12px\' }}>\\n                  <div style={{ display: \'flex\', justifyContent: \'space-between\', alignItems: \'center\', marginBottom: \'8px\' }}>\\n                    <h6 className=\\"mb-0\\">\\n                      Activity Feed\\n                      <Badge bg=\\"info\\" className=\\"ms-2\\" style={{ fontSize: \'10px\' }}>\\n                        {filteredActivities.length} / {activities.length} activities\\n                      </Badge>\\n                    </h6>\\n                    <span style={{ fontSize: \'11px\', color: \'#9ca3af\' }}>\\n                      {isPaused ? \'\\u23f8 Paused\' : `\\ud83d\\udd04 Updates every ${pollInterval}ms`}\\n                    </span>\\n                  </div>\\n                  {/* Activity Filter */}\\n                  <Form.Select\\n                    size=\\"sm\\"\\n                    value={activityFilter}\\n                    onChange={(e) => setActivityFilter(e.target.value)}\\n                    style={{\\n                      backgroundColor: \'#1a1d29\',\\n                      color: \'#e4e6eb\',\\n                      border: \'1px solid #3a3f52\',\\n                      fontSize: \'12px\'\\n                    }}\\n                  >\\n                    <option value=\\"all\\">All Activities</option>\\n                    <option value=\\"agent_spawned\\">Agent Spawned</option>\\n                    <option value=\\"agent_completed\\">Agent Completed</option>\\n                    <option value=\\"tool_use\\">Tool Use</option>\\n                    <option value=\\"iteration_started\\">Iteration Started</option>\\n                    <option value=\\"error\\">Errors</option>\\n                  </Form.Select>\\n                </div>\\n              </Card.Header>\\n              <Card.Body style={{ flex: 1, overflowY: \'auto\', padding: \'12px\' }}>\\n                <ActivityFeed activities={filteredActivities} />\\n              </Card.Body>\\n            </Card>\\n          </Col>\\n\\n          {/* Right Column - Agent States & Generated Files */}\\n          <Col md={4} style={{ height: \'100%\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n            {/* Current Agent Tasks */}\\n            <Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"light\\" className=\\"mb-3\\">\\n              <Card.Header\\n                style={{ cursor: \'pointer\' }}\\n                onClick={() => toggleSection(\'agents\')}\\n              >\\n                <div style={{ display: \'flex\', justifyContent: \'space-between\', alignItems: \'center\', marginBottom: \'8px\' }}>\\n                  <div>\\n                    <span style={{ marginRight: \'8px\' }}>\\n                      {sectionsCollapsed.agents ? \'\\u25b6\' : \'\\u25bc\'}\\n                    </span>\\n                    <span style={{ fontSize: \'14px\' }}>Agent Tasks</span>\\n                    <Badge bg=\\"warning\\" text=\\"dark\\" className=\\"ms-2\\" style={{ fontSize: \'10px\' }}>\\n                      {runningAgents} active\\n                    </Badge>\\n                    <Badge bg=\\"success\\" className=\\"ms-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'10px\' }}>\\n                      {completedAgents} done\\n                    </Badge>\\n                    {failedAgents > 0 && (\\n                      <Badge bg=\\"danger\\" className=\\"ms-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'10px\' }}>\\n                        {failedAgents} failed\\n                      </Badge>\\n                    )}\\n                  </div>\\n                </div>\\n                {!sectionsCollapsed.agents && (\\n                  <Form.Check\\n                    type=\\"switch\\"\\n                    label=\\"Hide completed\\"\\n                    checked={hideCompleted}\\n                    onChange={(e) => { e.stopPropagation(); setHideCompleted(!hideCompleted); }}\\n                    onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}\\n                    style={{\\n                      fontSize: \'12px\',\\n                      color: \'#9ca3af\',\\n                      cursor: \'pointer\'\\n                    }}\\n                  />\\n                )}\\n              </Card.Header>\\n              {!sectionsCollapsed.agents && (\\n                <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'400px\', overflowY: \'auto\', padding: \'12px\' }}>\\n                  {filteredAgentStates.length === 0 ? (\\n                    <div style={{ padding: \'20px\', textAlign: \'center\', color: \'#9ca3af\' }}>\\n                      {hideCompleted && Object.keys(agentStates).length > 0 ?\\n                        \'All agents completed (toggle filter to see them)\' :\\n                        \'No agents running. Start a task to see agent activity here.\'}\\n                    </div>\\n                  ) : (\\n                    filteredAgentStates.map(([agentId, state]) => (\\n                    <div\\n                      key={agentId}\\n                      style={{\\n                        marginBottom: \'12px\',\\n                        padding: \'12px\',\\n                        backgroundColor: \'#1a1d29\',\\n                        borderRadius: \'4px\',\\n                        border: \'1px solid #3a3f52\'\\n                      }}\\n                    >\\n                      <div style={{ display: \'flex\', justifyContent: \'space-between\', alignItems: \'center\', marginBottom: \'8px\' }}>\\n                        <strong style={{ fontSize: \'13px\' }}>{agentId}</strong>\\n                        <Badge\\n                          bg={\\n                            state.status === \'running\' ? \'warning\' :\\n                            state.status === \'completed\' ? \'success\' :\\n                            state.status === \'failed\' ? \'danger\' :\\n                            state.status === \'forever_failed\' ? \'dark\' :\\n                            state.status === \'needs_review\' ? \'info\' :\\n                            state.status === \'awaiting_user_input\' ? \'info\' :\\n                            state.status === \'stalled\' ? \'warning\' :\\n                            \'secondary\'\\n                          }\\n                          style={{ fontSize: \'10px\', ...(state.status === \'forever_failed\' ? { border: \'1px solid #dc3545\' } : {}) }}\\n                        >\\n                          {state.status === \'forever_failed\' ? \'\\u2620\\ufe0f TERMINATED\' : state.status}\\n                        </Badge>\\n                      </div>\\n\\n                      <div style={{ fontSize: \'12px\', color: \'#e4e6eb\', marginBottom: \'8px\' }}>\\n                        {state.current_task || \'Working...\'}\\n                      </div>\\n\\n                      {state.current_iteration > 0 && state.max_iterations > 0 && (\\n                        <div style={{ marginBottom: \'8px\' }}>\\n                          <div style={{ display: \'flex\', justifyContent: \'space-between\', fontSize: \'11px\', color: \'#9ca3af\', marginBottom: \'4px\' }}>\\n                            <span>Progress</span>\\n                            <span>{state.current_iteration} / {state.max_iterations}</span>\\n                          </div>\\n                          <div style={{\\n                            width: \'100%\',\\n                            height: \'4px\',\\n                            backgroundColor: \'#3a3f52\',\\n                            borderRadius: \'2px\',\\n                            overflow: \'hidden\'\\n                          }}>\\n                            <div style={{\\n                              width: `${(state.current_iteration / (state.max_iterations || 1)) * 100}%`,\\n                              height: \'100%\',\\n                              backgroundColor: state.status === \'completed\' ? \'#10b981\' : \'#fbbf24\',\\n                              transition: \'width 0.3s ease\'\\n                            }} />\\n                          </div>\\n                        </div>\\n                      )}\\n\\n                      <div style={{ fontSize: \'10px\', color: \'#6b7280\', marginTop: \'6px\' }}>\\n                        {state.started_at && (\\n                          <>Started: {new Date(state.started_at).toLocaleTimeString()}</>\\n                        )}\\n                        {state.status === \'completed\' && state.completed_at && (\\n                          <span> \\u2022 Completed: {new Date(state.completed_at).toLocaleTimeString()}</span>\\n                        )}\\n                      </div>\\n                    </div>\\n                  ))\\n                )}\\n              </Card.Body>\\n              )}\\n            </Card>\\n\\n            {/* Generated Files */}\\n            <Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"light\\">\\n              <Card.Header\\n                style={{ cursor: \'pointer\' }}\\n                onClick={() => toggleSection(\'files\')}\\n              >\\n                <div style={{ display: \'flex\', justifyContent: \'space-between\', alignItems: \'center\' }}>\\n                  <div>\\n                    <span style={{ marginRight: \'8px\' }}>\\n                      {sectionsCollapsed.files ? \'\\u25b6\' : \'\\u25bc\'}\\n                    </span>\\n                    <span style={{ fontSize: \'14px\' }}>Generated Files</span>\\n                    <Badge bg=\\"success\\" className=\\"ms-2\\" style={{ fontSize: \'10px\' }}>\\n                      {generatedFiles.length} files\\n                    </Badge>\\n                  </div>\\n                </div>\\n              </Card.Header>\\n              {!sectionsCollapsed.files && (\\n                <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'600px\', overflowY: \'auto\', padding: \'12px\' }}>\\n                  <GeneratedFiles files={generatedFiles} />\\n                </Card.Body>\\n              )}\\n            </Card>\\n          </Col>\\n        </Row>\\n        </Container>\\n        </>\\n      )}\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport default App;\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BoyGaSXSdYJr1aBtdeANqA', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/MetricsDashboard.jsx'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BoyGaSXSdYJr1aBtdeANqA', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\nimport { Container, Row, Col, Card, Table, Spinner, Form, Badge, ProgressBar } from \'react-bootstrap\';\\n\\nconst API_BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE || \'http://localhost:8001\';\\n\\nfunction MetricsDashboard() {\\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\\n  const [timeRange, setTimeRange] = useState(30);\\n  const [summary, setSummary] = useState(null);\\n  const [agentMetrics, setAgentMetrics] = useState(null);\\n  const [modelMetrics, setModelMetrics] = useState(null);\\n  const [complexityMetrics, setComplexityMetrics] = useState(null);\\n  const [errorAnalysis, setErrorAnalysis] = useState(null);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    fetchMetrics();\\n  }, [timeRange]);\\n\\n  const fetchMetrics = async () => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    try {\\n      const [summaryRes, agentRes, modelRes, complexityRes, errorRes] = await Promise.all([\\n        fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/metrics/summary?days=${timeRange}`),\\n        fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/metrics/agents?days=${timeRange}`),\\n        fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/metrics/models?days=${timeRange}`),\\n        fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/metrics/complexity?days=${timeRange}`),\\n        fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/metrics/errors?days=${timeRange}`)\\n      ]);\\n\\n      setSummary(await summaryRes.json());\\n      setAgentMetrics(await agentRes.json());\\n      setModelMetrics(await modelRes.json());\\n      setComplexityMetrics(await complexityRes.json());\\n      setErrorAnalysis(await errorRes.json());\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      console.error(\'Failed to fetch metrics:\', error);\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  if (loading) {\\n    return (\\n      <Container className=\\"mt-5 text-center\\">\\n        <Spinner animation=\\"border\\" variant=\\"primary\\" />\\n        <p className=\\"mt-3\\">Loading metrics...</p>\\n      </Container>\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  return (\\n    <Container fluid className=\\"mt-4\\">\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col>\\n          <h2>\\ud83d\\udcca Metrics Dashboard</h2>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col xs=\\"auto\\">\\n          <Form.Select\\n            value={timeRange}\\n            onChange={(e) => setTimeRange(parseInt(e.target.value))}\\n            style={{ width: \'150px\' }}\\n          >\\n            <option value={7}>Last 7 days</option>\\n            <option value={30}>Last 30 days</option>\\n            <option value={90}>Last 90 days</option>\\n          </Form.Select>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      {/* Summary Cards */}\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col md={3}>\\n          <Card bg=\\"primary\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n            <Card.Body>\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.75rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                Total Executions\\n              </h6>\\n              <h3 className=\\"mb-0\\">{summary?.overall?.total_executions || 0}</h3>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col md={3}>\\n          <Card bg=\\"success\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n            <Card.Body>\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.75rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                Success Rate\\n              </h6>\\n              <h3 className=\\"mb-0\\">{summary?.overall?.success_rate || 0}%</h3>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col md={3}>\\n          <Card bg=\\"info\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n            <Card.Body>\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.75rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                Unique Agents\\n              </h6>\\n              <h3 className=\\"mb-0\\">{summary?.overall?.unique_agents || 0}</h3>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col md={3}>\\n          <Card bg=\\"warning\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n            <Card.Body>\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.75rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                Avg Duration\\n              </h6>\\n              <h3 className=\\"mb-0\\">\\n                {summary?.overall?.avg_duration_ms\\n                  ? `${(summary.overall.avg_duration_ms / 1000).toFixed(1)}s`\\n                  : \'N/A\'}\\n              </h3>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col md={6}>\\n          {/* Most Active Agents */}\\n          <Card>\\n            <Card.Header>\\n              <strong>\\ud83d\\udd25 Most Active Agents</strong>\\n            </Card.Header>\\n            <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'300px\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n              <Table hover size=\\"sm\\" className=\\"mb-0\\">\\n                <thead>\\n                  <tr>\\n                    <th>Agent</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Executions</th>\\n                  </tr>\\n                </thead>\\n                <tbody>\\n                  {summary?.most_active_agents?.map((agent, idx) => (\\n                    <tr key={idx}>\\n                      <td>\\n                        <code style={{ fontSize: \'0.85rem\' }}>{agent.agent_name}</code>\\n                      </td>\\n                      <td className=\\"text-end\\">\\n                        <Badge bg=\\"primary\\">{agent.executions}</Badge>\\n                      </td>\\n                    </tr>\\n                  ))}\\n                </tbody>\\n              </Table>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n\\n        <Col md={6}>\\n          {/* Best Performing Agents */}\\n          <Card>\\n            <Card.Header>\\n              <strong>\\u2b50 Best Performing Agents</strong>\\n            </Card.Header>\\n            <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'300px\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n              <Table hover size=\\"sm\\" className=\\"mb-0\\">\\n                <thead>\\n                  <tr>\\n                    <th>Agent</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Success Rate</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Runs</th>\\n                  </tr>\\n                </thead>\\n                <tbody>\\n                  {summary?.best_performing_agents?.map((agent, idx) => (\\n                    <tr key={idx}>\\n                      <td>\\n                        <code style={{ fontSize: \'0.85rem\' }}>{agent.agent_name}</code>\\n                      </td>\\n                      <td className=\\"text-end\\">\\n                        <Badge\\n                          bg={agent.success_rate >= 90 ? \'success\' : agent.success_rate >= 70 ? \'warning\' : \'danger\'}\\n                        >\\n                          {agent.success_rate}%\\n                        </Badge>\\n                      </td>\\n                      <td className=\\"text-end\\">{agent.executions}</td>\\n                    </tr>\\n                  ))}\\n                </tbody>\\n              </Table>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      {/* Agent Performance */}\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col>\\n          <Card>\\n            <Card.Header>\\n              <strong>\\ud83e\\udd16 Agent Performance</strong>\\n            </Card.Header>\\n            <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'400px\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n              <Table hover size=\\"sm\\">\\n                <thead>\\n                  <tr>\\n                    <th>Agent</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Total</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Success</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Failed</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Success Rate</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Avg Duration</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Avg Iterations</th>\\n                  </tr>\\n                </thead>\\n                <tbody>\\n                  {agentMetrics?.agents?.map((agent, idx) => (\\n                    <tr key={idx}>\\n                      <td>\\n                        <code style={{ fontSize: \'0.85rem\' }}>{agent.agent_name}</code>\\n                      </td>\\n                      <td className=\\"text-end\\">{agent.total_executions}</td>\\n                      <td className=\\"text-end\\">\\n                        <span style={{ color: \'#10b981\' }}>{agent.successful}</span>\\n                      </td>\\n                      <td className=\\"text-end\\">\\n                        <span style={{ color: \'#ef4444\' }}>{agent.failed}</span>\\n                      </td>\\n                      <td className=\\"text-end\\">\\n                        <div style={{ width: \'100px\', display: \'inline-block\' }}>\\n                          <ProgressBar\\n                            now={agent.success_rate || 0}\\n                            min={0}\\n                            max={100}\\n                            variant={(agent.success_rate || 0) >= 90 ? \'success\' : (agent.success_rate || 0) >= 70 ? \'warning\' : \'danger\'}\\n                            style={{ height: \'20px\' }}\\n                            label={`${agent.success_rate || 0}%`}\\n                          />\\n                        </div>\\n                      </td>\\n                      <td className=\\"text-end\\">\\n                        {agent.avg_duration_ms ? `${(agent.avg_duration_ms / 1000).toFixed(1)}s` : \'N/A\'}\\n                      </td>\\n                      <td className=\\"text-end\\">{agent.avg_iterations}</td>\\n                    </tr>\\n                  ))}\\n                </tbody>\\n              </Table>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col md={6}>\\n          {/* Model Performance */}\\n          <Card>\\n            <Card.Header>\\n              <strong>\\ud83e\\udde0 Model Performance</strong>\\n            </Card.Header>\\n            <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'400px\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n              <Table hover size=\\"sm\\">\\n                <thead>\\n                  <tr>\\n                    <th>Model</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Runs</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Success Rate</th>\\n                  </tr>\\n                </thead>\\n                <tbody>\\n                  {modelMetrics?.models?.map((model, idx) => {\\n                    const modelName = model.model_used.includes(\'sonnet\') ? \'Sonnet 4.5\' :\\n                                    model.model_used.includes(\'opus\') ? \'Opus 4.5\' :\\n                                    model.model_used.includes(\'haiku\') ? \'Haiku 3.5\' : model.model_used;\\n                    return (\\n                      <tr key={idx}>\\n                        <td>\\n                          <Badge bg=\\"secondary\\">{modelName}</Badge>\\n                        </td>\\n                        <td className=\\"text-end\\">{model.total_executions}</td>\\n                        <td className=\\"text-end\\">\\n                          <div style={{ width: \'100px\', display: \'inline-block\' }}>\\n                            <ProgressBar\\n                              now={model.success_rate || 0}\\n                              min={0}\\n                              max={100}\\n                              variant={(model.success_rate || 0) >= 90 ? \'success\' : \'warning\'}\\n                              style={{ height: \'20px\' }}\\n                              label={`${model.success_rate || 0}%`}\\n                            />\\n                          </div>\\n                        </td>\\n                      </tr>\\n                    );\\n                  })}\\n                </tbody>\\n              </Table>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n\\n        <Col md={6}>\\n          {/* Complexity Performance */}\\n          <Card>\\n            <Card.Header>\\n              <strong>\\ud83d\\udcc8 Performance by Complexity</strong>\\n            </Card.Header>\\n            <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'400px\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n              <Table hover size=\\"sm\\">\\n                <thead>\\n                  <tr>\\n                    <th>Complexity</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Runs</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Success Rate</th>\\n                    <th className=\\"text-end\\">Avg Duration</th>\\n                  </tr>\\n                </thead>\\n                <tbody>\\n                  {complexityMetrics?.complexities?.map((item, idx) => (\\n                    <tr key={idx}>\\n                      <td>\\n                        <Badge\\n                          bg={item.task_complexity === \'simple\' ? \'success\' :\\n                              item.task_complexity === \'creative\' ? \'warning\' : \'danger\'}\\n                        >\\n                          {item.task_complexity || \'unknown\'}\\n                        </Badge>\\n                      </td>\\n                      <td className=\\"text-end\\">{item.total_executions}</td>\\n                      <td className=\\"text-end\\">\\n                        <div style={{ width: \'100px\', display: \'inline-block\' }}>\\n                          <ProgressBar\\n                            now={item.success_rate || 0}\\n                            min={0}\\n                            max={100}\\n                            variant=\\"info\\"\\n                            style={{ height: \'20px\' }}\\n                            label={`${item.success_rate || 0}%`}\\n                          />\\n                        </div>\\n                      </td>\\n                      <td className=\\"text-end\\">\\n                        {item.avg_duration_ms ? `${(item.avg_duration_ms / 1000).toFixed(1)}s` : \'N/A\'}\\n                      </td>\\n                    </tr>\\n                  ))}\\n                </tbody>\\n              </Table>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      {/* Error Analysis */}\\n      {errorAnalysis?.errors && errorAnalysis.errors.length > 0 && (\\n        <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n          <Col>\\n            <Card>\\n              <Card.Header>\\n                <strong>\\u26a0\\ufe0f Error Analysis</strong>\\n              </Card.Header>\\n              <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'400px\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n                <Table hover size=\\"sm\\">\\n                  <thead>\\n                    <tr>\\n                      <th>Error Type</th>\\n                      <th>Agent</th>\\n                      <th className=\\"text-end\\">Occurrences</th>\\n                      <th className=\\"text-end\\">Avg Time Before Failure</th>\\n                    </tr>\\n                  </thead>\\n                  <tbody>\\n                    {errorAnalysis.errors.map((error, idx) => (\\n                      <tr key={idx}>\\n                        <td>\\n                          <code style={{ fontSize: \'0.85rem\', color: \'#ef4444\' }}>\\n                            {error.error_type}\\n                          </code>\\n                        </td>\\n                        <td>\\n                          <code style={{ fontSize: \'0.85rem\' }}>{error.agent_name}</code>\\n                        </td>\\n                        <td className=\\"text-end\\">\\n                          <Badge bg=\\"danger\\">{error.occurrences}</Badge>\\n                        </td>\\n                        <td className=\\"text-end\\">\\n                          {error.avg_duration_before_failure\\n                            ? `${(error.avg_duration_before_failure / 1000).toFixed(1)}s`\\n                            : \'N/A\'}\\n                        </td>\\n                      </tr>\\n                    ))}\\n                  </tbody>\\n                </Table>\\n              </Card.Body>\\n            </Card>\\n          </Col>\\n        </Row>\\n      )}\\n\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col>\\n          <Card bg=\\"light\\">\\n            <Card.Body>\\n              <p className=\\"mb-0 text-muted\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.875rem\' }}>\\n                <strong>Note:</strong> Metrics are calculated based on agent executions in the last {timeRange} days.\\n                Use the dropdown above to change the time range.\\n              </p>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n    </Container>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport default MetricsDashboard;\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Ec8DapoSRZnF9reNShAR2b', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '7d3fdba2', 'category': 'decision', 'note': "Initial investigation complete. Found issue is NOT with metrics pane agent display - the metrics pane shows summary data by agent type, not individual agents. User's confusion is about activity feed filtering which has limited dropdown options that don't show all new agent types. Will create requirements to fix activity feed filtering system."}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Ec8DapoSRZnF9reNShAR2b', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SVqBGUB2fyBMgcfLwZAUJ8', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'content': '# Fix UI Panes Against Requirements Analysis\n\n## Problem Description\nUser reports not seeing new agents in the metrics pane, but investigation reveals the actual issue is broader: multiple UI panes don\'t properly reflect the current system state and available agent types. The activity feed filtering is particularly limited and doesn\'t show all agent activity types.\n\n## Current State Analysis\n\n### Issues Identified\n\n**1. Activity Feed Filter Limitations**\n- Hardcoded dropdown options: "all", "agent_spawned", "agent_completed", "tool_use", "iteration_started", "error"\n- Missing many actual activity types from the system\n- Filter logic uses exact string matching only\n- Cannot filter by agent states (failed, error, etc.)\n- No way to see new agent types that have been added to the system\n\n**2. Metrics Pane Functionality**\n- Actually works correctly - shows aggregate metrics by agent performance\n- User confusion may be about expecting individual agent visibility vs. aggregate metrics\n- Missing some newer agent types in the data aggregation\n\n**3. Agent States Display**\n- Shows running agents correctly but filtering is basic\n- Limited visibility into failed states and error details\n- No filtering by agent type/category\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\nThe UI was designed when fewer agent types existed and hasn\'t been updated to handle the expanded agent ecosystem. The filtering systems are static rather than dynamic.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### R1: Dynamic Activity Feed Filtering\n**Must implement dynamic filter generation**:\n- Scan actual activities to determine available activity types\n- Generate filter options based on real data, not hardcoded values\n- Support semantic groupings:\n  - Agent Lifecycle: spawned, started, completed, failed\n  - Iterations: started, completed\n  - Tool Usage: tool_use_started, tool_use_completed, tool_use_failed\n  - Communications: message, question, answer\n  - System Events: status_change, task_update\n  - Errors/Issues: any activity with error indicators\n\n### R2: Enhanced Agent Type Visibility\n**Must show all agent types currently in system**:\n- Executive Director\n- Development Manager\n- System Architect\n- TDD Coordinator\n- Code Writer\n- Code Tester\n- Any newly spawned agent types\n\n### R3: Real-time Filter Updates\n**Must dynamically update filters**:\n- When new activity types appear, add them to filters\n- When new agent types are spawned, show them in relevant panes\n- Count activities per filter option for user clarity\n\n### R4: Improved Error/Failed State Visibility\n**Must better highlight problems**:\n- Failed agents prominently displayed\n- Error activities easy to filter and find\n- Clear visual distinction between different failure modes\n\n### R5: Metrics Pane Agent Coverage  \n**Must ensure metrics include all agent types**:\n- Verify backend aggregation includes all agent types\n- Display newer agent types in performance tables\n- Show agent type distribution in summary\n\n## Technical Implementation Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Activity Feed Enhancement\n1. **Dynamic Filter Generation**\n   - Scan activities array for unique activity_type values\n   - Create semantic groupings for related activity types\n   - Build filter dropdown dynamically\n\n2. **Smart Filter Logic**\n   - Replace exact string matching with category-based filtering\n   - Support multiple activity types per filter\n   - Handle special cases (error detection, agent state filtering)\n\n3. **Activity Count Display**\n   - Show count of activities per filter option\n   - Update counts as new activities arrive\n\n### Phase 2: Metrics Pane Verification\n1. **Backend API Check**\n   - Verify all agent types are included in metrics aggregation\n   - Ensure new agent types appear in performance tables\n\n2. **Frontend Display Enhancement**\n   - Improve agent name display and grouping\n   - Add agent type categorization in metrics views\n\n### Phase 3: Agent States Enhancement\n1. **Enhanced Agent Type Filtering**\n   - Add filtering by agent category (leadership, coordinators, developers, testers)\n   - Show agent type in agent task display\n\n2. **Better Error State Display**\n   - Highlight failed agents more prominently\n   - Show error details and failure reasons\n   - Add quick filter for "problem agents"\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n### Functional Requirements\n1. **Activity feed shows all activity types present in system**\n2. **User can filter by semantic categories (errors, agent lifecycle, etc.)**\n3. **All spawned agent types visible in relevant UI panes**\n4. **Failed/error states clearly visible and filterable**\n5. **Metrics pane includes performance data for all agent types**\n\n### User Experience Requirements\n1. **Filters are intuitive and self-explanatory**\n2. **No confusion about where to find specific agent information**\n3. **Clear visual indication of system problems/failures**\n4. **Filters show activity counts for context**\n\n### Technical Requirements\n1. **Dynamic filter generation based on actual data**\n2. **Performant with 200+ activities**\n3. **Real-time updates as new agent types appear**\n4. **Backward compatible with existing activity data**\n\n## Implementation Priority\n1. **HIGH**: Activity feed dynamic filtering (addresses primary user complaint)\n2. **MEDIUM**: Agent type visibility improvements\n3. **MEDIUM**: Enhanced error state display\n4. **LOW**: Metrics pane verification (likely already working)\n\n## Out of Scope\n- Changes to backend activity tracking\n- New activity types creation\n- UI redesign or layout changes\n- Search functionality within panes\n\n## Constraints\n- Must maintain existing UI performance\n- Cannot break existing polling/update logic\n- Must work with current activity data structure\n- No backend API changes required\n\n## Assumptions\n- Activity data contains consistent activity_type field\n- Agent spawning creates trackable activities\n- Current metrics backend includes all agent types\n- User wants to see real-time agent activity, not just aggregated metrics'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SVqBGUB2fyBMgcfLwZAUJ8', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260115_013537.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260115_013537.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Pi3G9jvzS8PeCpTwvHQUaV', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '7d3fdba2', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': "Requirements analysis complete. Created comprehensive requirements document identifying the real issue: activity feed filtering is hardcoded and doesn't show new agent types. Plan prioritizes dynamic filter generation as high priority solution."}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Pi3G9jvzS8PeCpTwvHQUaV', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_019MQYYx3jEGNYLmFGwQTmkN', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': '7d3fdba2', 'assigned_to': 'leadership/development_manager', 'description': 'Implement dynamic activity feed filtering and enhance agent visibility across all UI panes to properly show new agent types and improve error state visibility'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019MQYYx3jEGNYLmFGwQTmkN', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "077c775a", "message": "Added task: Implement dynamic activity feed filtering and enhance agent visibility across all UI panes to properly show new agent types and improve error state visibility"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Pyt