{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 01:36:32", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-518ab5ca-bcce-4d95-8454-13f868192be8', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014a8EAypLP5K7mQ29mRbiRH', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014a8EAypLP5K7mQ29mRbiRH', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Token Tracking Implementation - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name**: Token Tracking Implementation  \\n**Objective**: Implement comprehensive token tracking for all API calls in the ensemble agent system to enable accurate cost calculation and performance monitoring.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nThe ensemble agent system currently passes `tokens_used=None` to the activity tracker for all API calls. This prevents accurate cost calculation, performance analysis, and resource optimization. Token usage data from the Anthropic API responses needs to be extracted, stored, and made available through existing endpoints.\\n\\n## Vision Statement\\n\\nEnable complete visibility into token usage across the ensemble agent system by capturing, storing, and exposing real token consumption data from every API call, facilitating accurate cost tracking, performance optimization, and resource management.\\n\\n## Core Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Token Extraction from API Responses\\n- **Requirement**: Extract actual token counts from Anthropic API responses in `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\\n- **Details**: \\n  - Capture `input_tokens` and `output_tokens` from `response.usage`\\n  - Maintain running totals for each agent execution\\n  - Log token usage per iteration for debugging\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  - Every API call records actual token usage instead of `None`\\n  - Token counts are accumulated across iterations\\n  - Debug logging shows per-iteration token usage\\n\\n### 2. ActivityTracker Token Storage\\n- **Requirement**: Update `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` to store comprehensive token data\\n- **Details**:\\n  - Add `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `total_tokens` parameters to relevant methods\\n  - Store token data in agent state and hierarchy records\\n  - Maintain token tracking in activity records\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  - `record_agent_completed()` accepts and stores token parameters\\n  - Agent states include token usage data\\n  - Activity records contain token information\\n\\n### 3. Cost Calculation Enhancement\\n- **Requirement**: Integrate real token data into cost calculations\\n- **Details**:\\n  - Use actual token counts instead of estimates\\n  - Support per-agent and aggregate cost calculations\\n  - Maintain existing cost calculation interfaces\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  - Cost estimates use real token data\\n  - Agent completion records include accurate costs\\n  - Existing cost calculation functionality preserved\\n\\n### 4. API Endpoint Exposure\\n- **Requirement**: Expose token metrics through existing API endpoints in `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\\n- **Details**:\\n  - Include token data in agent state responses\\n  - Add token aggregation to request timeline data\\n  - Maintain backward compatibility with existing endpoints\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  - `/api/agents/state` endpoint returns token usage data\\n  - `/api/requests/{request_id}/timeline` includes token metrics\\n  - Existing API contracts unchanged\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Performance Requirements\\n- Token extraction adds minimal latency to API calls\\n- Token data storage does not significantly impact memory usage\\n- API responses include token data without performance degradation\\n\\n### Data Requirements\\n- Token counts stored as integers\\n- Support for input, output, and total token tracking\\n- Historical token data preserved across agent executions\\n\\n### Integration Requirements\\n- No breaking changes to existing interfaces\\n- Backward compatibility with current cost calculation system\\n- Seamless integration with existing activity tracking\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n### Scope Limitations\\n- **Backend-only implementation** - no UI modifications required\\n- Focus on Anthropic API token extraction only\\n- No changes to existing agent definitions or tool interfaces\\n\\n### Technical Constraints\\n- Must use existing ActivityTracker infrastructure\\n- Cannot modify agent execution flow significantly\\n- Must maintain existing error handling and resilience patterns\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n\\n1. **`src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`**\\n   - Extract token usage from `response.usage` \\n   - Pass real token data to activity tracker\\n   - Update cost calculation calls\\n\\n2. **`src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`**\\n   - Add token parameters to `record_agent_completed()` method\\n   - Store token data in agent states and hierarchy\\n   - Include token information in activity records\\n\\n3. **`src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`** (if needed)\\n   - Ensure token data flows through API endpoints\\n   - Add token aggregation to timeline responses\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n### Primary Success Criteria\\n1. **Token Extraction**: Every API call records actual token usage\\n2. **Data Storage**: Token counts visible in agent state API responses\\n3. **Cost Accuracy**: Cost calculations use real token data instead of estimates\\n4. **API Visibility**: Token metrics available through existing endpoints\\n\\n### Testing Criteria\\n1. **Unit Tests**: Verify token extraction from mock API responses\\n2. **Integration Tests**: Confirm token data flows through activity tracker\\n3. **API Tests**: Validate token data appears in endpoint responses\\n4. **Cost Tests**: Verify cost calculations use real token data\\n\\n### Performance Criteria\\n- Token extraction adds <1ms latency per API call\\n- Token storage increases memory usage by <5%\\n- API response times remain within current SLAs\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n### Phase 1: Runtime Token Extraction\\n- Modify `AgentRuntime.execute()` to extract tokens from `response.usage`\\n- Update token accumulation logic\\n- Add debug logging for token usage\\n\\n### Phase 2: ActivityTracker Integration  \\n- Update `record_agent_completed()` method signature\\n- Store token data in agent states and hierarchy\\n- Ensure backward compatibility\\n\\n### Phase 3: Cost Calculation Update\\n- Integrate real token data into cost calculations\\n- Update cost estimation logic\\n- Verify cost accuracy improvements\\n\\n### Phase 4: API Endpoint Integration\\n- Ensure token data flows through existing endpoints\\n- Add token aggregation where appropriate\\n- Validate API response structures\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Anthropic API Structure**: Response objects consistently include `usage.input_tokens` and `usage.output_tokens`\\n2. **Existing Infrastructure**: Current ActivityTracker and cost calculation systems can accommodate token data\\n3. **Performance Impact**: Token extraction overhead is negligible compared to API call latency\\n4. **Backward Compatibility**: Existing systems can handle additional token parameters gracefully\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- UI modifications or new frontend components\\n- Token tracking for non-Anthropic API calls\\n- Historical data migration for existing records\\n- Token usage alerts or monitoring systems\\n- Token-based rate limiting or quota management\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- Anthropic Python SDK with usage tracking support\\n- Existing ActivityTracker infrastructure\\n- Current cost calculation system\\n- FastAPI backend endpoints\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n\\n### Technical Risks\\n- **API Response Structure Changes**: Monitor Anthropic API documentation for changes\\n- **Performance Degradation**: Implement efficient token extraction and storage\\n- **Memory Usage**: Use appropriate data types and cleanup strategies\\n\\n### Implementation Risks\\n- **Breaking Changes**: Maintain backward compatibility throughout implementation\\n- **Data Integrity**: Ensure token data consistency across all tracking points\\n- **Error Handling**: Graceful degradation when token data unavailable"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015pH45pe2mRDhoNAkjL4M7D', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Token Tracking Implementation - Architecture Proposal\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\n### High-Level Design\nThis architecture implements comprehensive token tracking across the ensemble agent system using a **data flow enhancement pattern**. Rather than restructuring the existing system, we augment the current agent runtime → activity tracker → API endpoint flow with token data collection, storage, and exposure.\n\n### Architecture Pattern\n**Pipeline Enhancement Pattern** - We enhance the existing three-tier pipeline:\n1. **Data Collection Layer**: Extract tokens from API responses\n2. **Storage Layer**: Augment existing ActivityTracker with token persistence \n3. **Exposure Layer**: Surface token data through existing API endpoints\n\n**Rationale**: This approach minimizes risk by preserving existing interfaces while adding the required functionality. It leverages proven patterns already in the codebase and maintains backward compatibility.\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n### Core Technologies\n- **Python 3.8+**: Existing runtime language\n- **FastAPI**: Existing web framework for API endpoints\n- **Anthropic Python SDK**: For API response parsing\n- **In-Memory Storage**: Existing ActivityTracker storage pattern\n\n### Libraries and Dependencies\n- **anthropic**: Already present, provides `response.usage` data structure\n- **typing**: For type hints on new token parameters\n- **logging**: For debug output of token usage\n- **dataclasses/dict**: For token data structures\n\n**Rationale**: We use 100% existing technologies to minimize dependencies and integration risk. The Anthropic SDK already provides the token data we need, so no additional parsing libraries are required.\n\n### What We\'re NOT Adding\n- **New databases**: Using existing in-memory tracking\n- **New web frameworks**: Leveraging existing FastAPI setup\n- **New monitoring tools**: Basic logging for observability\n\n## System Components\n\n### Component Breakdown\n\n#### 1. Token Extractor (New Component)\n**Location**: `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\n**Responsibility**: \n- Extract `input_tokens` and `output_tokens` from `response.usage`\n- Accumulate tokens across agent iterations\n- Provide token totals for activity tracking\n\n**Interface**:\n```python\nclass TokenUsage:\n    input_tokens: int\n    output_tokens: int\n    total_tokens: int\n    \n    def accumulate(self, other: TokenUsage) -> TokenUsage\n```\n\n#### 2. Enhanced Activity Tracker (Modified Component)\n**Location**: `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\n**Responsibility**:\n- Store token data alongside existing agent state\n- Maintain backward compatibility\n- Provide token data for API responses\n\n**Key Changes**:\n- Add optional token parameters to `record_agent_completed()`\n- Extend agent state dictionaries with token data\n- Maintain token information in activity records\n\n#### 3. API Response Enhancer (Modified Component)  \n**Location**: `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\n**Responsibility**:\n- Include token data in existing endpoint responses\n- Aggregate tokens for timeline views\n- Ensure backward compatibility\n\n### Data Flow Diagram\n\n```\n┌─────────────────┐    ┌──────────────────┐    ┌─────────────────┐\n│   Agent Runtime │    │ Activity Tracker │    │   API Endpoint  │\n│                 │    │                  │    │                 │\n│ 1. Execute API  │───▶│ 2. Store Agent   │───▶│ 3. Expose Data  │\n│ 2. Extract      │    │    State + Tokens│    │    + Tokens     │\n│    Tokens       │    │                  │    │                 │\n└─────────────────┘    └──────────────────┘    └─────────────────┘\n         │                        │                        │\n         ▼                        ▼                        ▼\n┌─────────────────┐    ┌──────────────────┐    ┌─────────────────┐\n│ TokenUsage      │    │ Enhanced Agent   │    │ Token-Enriched  │\n│ - input_tokens  │    │ State Dict:      │    │ API Responses   │\n│ - output_tokens │    │ + token_usage    │    │                 │\n│ - total_tokens  │    │ + cost_data      │    │                 │\n└─────────────────┘    └──────────────────┘    └─────────────────┘\n```\n\n## File/Directory Structure\n\nNo new directories needed. Modifications to existing files:\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── runtime/\n│   └── agents/\n│       ├── runtime.py              # Token extraction logic\n│       └── activity_tracker.py     # Token storage enhancement\n└── field/\n    └── ensemble_ui/\n        └── backend/\n            └── main.py             # Token exposure (if needed)\n```\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Token Data Structure\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass TokenUsage:\n    input_tokens: int = 0\n    output_tokens: int = 0\n    \n    @property\n    def total_tokens(self) -> int:\n        return self.input_tokens + self.output_tokens\n    \n    def accumulate(self, other: \'TokenUsage\') -> \'TokenUsage\':\n        return TokenUsage(\n            input_tokens=self.input_tokens + other.input_tokens,\n            output_tokens=self.output_tokens + other.output_tokens\n        )\n```\n\n### Enhanced Agent State\n```python\n# Current agent state (preserved)\nagent_state = {\n    "agent_id": "...",\n    "status": "completed", \n    "result": "...",\n    "cost": 0.05,\n    # ... existing fields\n}\n\n# Enhanced agent state (new fields added)\nenhanced_agent_state = {\n    **agent_state,  # All existing fields preserved\n    "token_usage": {\n        "input_tokens": 150,\n        "output_tokens": 75, \n        "total_tokens": 225\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### API Response Structure\n```json\n{\n  "agent_states": [\n    {\n      "agent_id": "code_writer_001",\n      "status": "completed",\n      "result": "...",\n      "cost": 0.05,\n      "token_usage": {\n        "input_tokens": 150,\n        "output_tokens": 75,\n        "total_tokens": 225\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## API Design\n\n### Endpoint Modifications\n\n#### `/api/agents/state` (Enhanced)\n**Current Response**: Agent states without token data\n**New Response**: Existing response + token usage data\n**Backward Compatibility**: ✅ All existing fields preserved\n\n#### `/api/requests/{request_id}/timeline` (Enhanced) \n**Current Response**: Timeline events with cost estimates\n**New Response**: Existing response + actual token counts\n**Backward Compatibility**: ✅ All existing fields preserved\n\n### Authentication\nNo changes - uses existing JWT/session authentication\n\n## Deployment Strategy\n\n### Development Environment\n- No additional setup required\n- Uses existing Python environment and dependencies\n- Changes are code-only, no infrastructure modifications\n\n### Production Deployment\n- **Zero-downtime deployment**: Changes are additive only\n- **Rollback safety**: All changes are backward compatible\n- **Monitoring**: Use existing logging infrastructure\n\n### CI/CD Considerations\n- **Unit tests**: Test token extraction from mock responses\n- **Integration tests**: Verify end-to-end token flow\n- **Regression tests**: Ensure existing functionality unchanged\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Testing Approach\n```python\n# Test token extraction\ndef test_extract_tokens_from_anthropic_response():\n    mock_response = create_mock_response(\n        input_tokens=100, \n        output_tokens=50\n    )\n    tokens = extract_tokens(mock_response)\n    assert tokens.input_tokens == 100\n    assert tokens.output_tokens == 50\n    assert tokens.total_tokens == 150\n\n# Test token accumulation  \ndef test_accumulate_tokens():\n    usage1 = TokenUsage(100, 50)\n    usage2 = TokenUsage(75, 25)\n    total = usage1.accumulate(usage2)\n    assert total.total_tokens == 250\n```\n\n### Integration Testing Approach\n```python\n# Test end-to-end token flow\ndef test_token_flow_through_system():\n    # Execute agent with mock API\n    result = execute_agent_with_mocks()\n    \n    # Verify tokens stored in activity tracker\n    agent_state = activity_tracker.get_agent_state(agent_id)\n    assert "token_usage" in agent_state\n    \n    # Verify tokens in API response\n    api_response = get_agent_state_api()\n    assert api_response["token_usage"]["total_tokens"] > 0\n```\n\n### Requirement Verification Tests\n- **Token Extraction**: Verify every API call records actual tokens\n- **Cost Accuracy**: Verify costs use real token data\n- **API Visibility**: Verify tokens appear in endpoint responses  \n- **Performance**: Verify <1ms latency impact\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### Alternative 1: New Token Service\n**Approach**: Create separate token tracking service\n**Rejected**: Over-engineering for the requirements\n**Trade-offs**: More complex, harder to maintain, unnecessary\n\n### Alternative 2: Database Token Storage\n**Approach**: Store token data in persistent database\n**Rejected**: Requirements specify using existing infrastructure\n**Trade-offs**: More durable but adds complexity and dependencies\n\n### Alternative 3: Async Token Logging\n**Approach**: Log tokens asynchronously to avoid latency\n**Rejected**: Requirements need real-time cost calculation\n**Trade-offs**: Better performance but delayed data availability\n\n### Alternative 4: Token Middleware Pattern\n**Approach**: Intercept all API calls with middleware\n**Rejected**: More invasive changes, harder to debug\n**Trade-offs**: Cleaner separation but more complex integration\n\n## Chosen Approach: Minimal Enhancement Pattern\n**Why chosen**:\n- ✅ Preserves existing architecture and interfaces\n- ✅ Minimal risk and complexity\n- ✅ Easy to test and rollback\n- ✅ Meets all requirements without over-engineering\n- ✅ Uses proven patterns already in codebase\n\n## Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Technical Risks\n\n**Risk**: Anthropic API response structure changes\n**Mitigation**: \n- Defensive parsing with try-catch blocks\n- Default to 0 tokens if extraction fails\n- Log warnings when token data unavailable\n\n**Risk**: Performance impact on API calls\n**Mitigation**:\n- Benchmark token extraction (should be <0.1ms)\n- Use efficient data structures (integers, simple objects)\n- Monitor API call latencies\n\n**Risk**: Memory usage increase  \n**Mitigation**:\n- Use integers instead of complex objects\n- Clean up token data with agent states\n- Monitor memory usage in production\n\n### Integration Risks\n\n**Risk**: Breaking existing cost calculations\n**Mitigation**:\n- Maintain existing cost calculation interfaces\n- Default to current estimates if token data unavailable\n- Extensive regression testing\n\n**Risk**: API response compatibility issues\n**Mitigation**: \n- Add token data as new optional fields\n- Preserve all existing response structure\n- Test with existing API clients\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Token Extraction (Week 1)\n**Files**: `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\n**Tasks**:\n- Add `TokenUsage` data class\n- Extract tokens from `response.usage` \n- Accumulate tokens across iterations\n- Add debug logging\n\n**Validation**: Unit tests verify token extraction\n\n### Phase 2: Activity Tracker Enhancement (Week 1)\n**Files**: `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\n**Tasks**:\n- Add optional token parameters to `record_agent_completed()`\n- Store token data in agent state dictionaries\n- Maintain backward compatibility\n\n**Validation**: Integration tests verify token storage\n\n### Phase 3: Cost Integration (Week 2)\n**Files**: `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\n**Tasks**:\n- Pass real token data to cost calculations\n- Update cost estimation logic\n- Ensure fallback to estimates\n\n**Validation**: Cost accuracy tests\n\n### Phase 4: API Enhancement (Week 2)  \n**Files**: `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\n**Tasks**:\n- Verify token data flows through endpoints\n- Add token aggregation for timeline\n- Test API responses\n\n**Validation**: API tests verify token exposure\n\n## Open Questions\n\n### Trade-offs Requiring User Input\n\n1. **Error Handling Strategy**: \n   - **Option A**: Fail silently, default to 0 tokens\n   - **Option B**: Log warnings but continue execution\n   - **Option C**: Raise exceptions for missing token data\n   - **Recommendation**: Option B for observability without brittleness\n\n2. **Token Precision**:\n   - **Option A**: Store exact tokens as integers\n   - **Option B**: Round to nearest 100 for display\n   - **Recommendation**: Option A for accuracy\n\n3. **Historical Data**:\n   - **Option A**: Token data only for new executions\n   - **Option B**: Attempt to estimate tokens for historical data\n   - **Recommendation**: Option A (out of scope per requirements)\n\n### Technical Decisions Needing Confirmation\n\n1. **Token Storage Format**: Simple integers vs structured objects?\n2. **Cost Calculation Priority**: Real tokens vs estimates when both available?\n3. **Debug Logging Level**: Per-iteration vs per-agent vs both?\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n### Functional Success\n- [ ] Every API call records actual token usage (not None)\n- [ ] Agent state API responses include token data\n- [ ] Cost calculations use real token counts\n- [ ] Backward compatibility maintained (0 breaking changes)\n\n### Performance Success  \n- [ ] Token extraction adds <1ms per API call\n- [ ] Memory usage increase <5%\n- [ ] API response times within existing SLAs\n\n### Quality Success\n- [ ] 100% unit test coverage for new token logic\n- [ ] Integration tests verify end-to-end token flow\n- [ ] Regression tests pass for existing functionality\n\nThis architecture provides a robust, maintainable solution that meets all requirements while minimizing risk and complexity through careful enhancement of existing systems.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015pH45pe2mRDhoNAkjL4M7D', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260115_013632.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260115_013632.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.6\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully analyzed the UI enhancement requirements and designed a focused, low-risk architecture that leverages existing React patterns while adding the requested whimsical naming and leaderboard...\n- I successfully analyzed the theme switcher requirements and designed a performance-focused architecture that leverages CSS Custom Properties for instant theme switching. The proposal addresses all fun...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including