{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 01:47:09", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-6946d30b-0eb3-4a0d-a014-9120477f4df0', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "Request Cleanup System Improvement"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DsFzgyxPbLjTcxpVcfuLov', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DsFzgyxPbLjTcxpVcfuLov', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Request Cleanup System Improvement Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nEnhance the ActivityTracker\'s request cleanup mechanism to resolve memory growth issues and implement robust activity filtering.\\n\\n## Context\\n- Current `clear_request()` method in ActivityTracker is incomplete\\n- No effective request filtering mechanism exists\\n- Activities accumulate without proper cleanup\\n- Causing significant memory usage growth\\n\\n## Detailed Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Request Cleanup Implementation\\n- Complete `clear_request()` method in `activity_tracker.py`\\n- Fully remove request-specific data from tracking system\\n- Ensure no orphaned or partial data remains\\n\\n### 2. Activity Filtering\\n- Implement filtering mechanism by `request_id`\\n- Allow selective retrieval and deletion of activities\\n- Support complex query operations on activity metadata\\n\\n### 3. Automatic Cleanup Mechanism\\n- Add configurable activity retention policy\\n- Automatically remove activities older than specified threshold\\n- Configurable retention period (default and per-request)\\n- Preserve active request data during cleanup\\n\\n### 4. Performance and Stability\\n- Maintain system performance during cleanup operations\\n- Prevent memory leaks\\n- Minimal performance overhead\\n- Ensure cleanup does not interrupt ongoing activities\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- \\u2705 `clear_request()` completely removes request data\\n- \\u2705 Implement robust activity filtering by `request_id`\\n- \\u2705 Automatic cleanup of old activities\\n- \\u2705 Configurable retention periods\\n- \\u2705 Memory usage remains stable\\n- \\u2705 No data loss for active requests\\n- \\u2705 Existing system functionality unaffected\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Modify: `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\\n- TDD Approach: Write tests first, then implementation\\n- Maintain backward compatibility\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Retention period will be configurable (default: 7 days)\\n- Cleanup will run as background task\\n- No performance degradation during cleanup\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Complete system rewrite\\n- Changes to external API\\n- Modifications to unrelated tracking components\\n\\n## Potential Risks\\n- Incomplete data removal\\n- Performance impact during cleanup\\n- Unintended data loss\\n\\n## Recommended Approach\\n1. Write comprehensive test cases\\n2. Implement filtering mechanism\\n3. Develop cleanup algorithm\\n4. Add configuration options\\n5. Perform extensive performance testing"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VtbfNpEd1oEmLq2CopxjbU', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Request Cleanup System Architecture Proposal\n\n## A. Architecture Overview\n\n### Design Pattern: Enhanced Service Module with Background Processing\nThe Request Cleanup System will be implemented as an enhanced service module within the existing ActivityTracker, leveraging a modular, configurable approach to activity management and cleanup.\n\n## B. Tech Stack\n\n### Core Technologies\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\n- **Concurrency**: `asyncio` for background processing\n- **Testing**: `pytest` with `hypothesis` for property-based testing\n\n### Key Libraries\n- `typing` for type hints\n- `dataclasses` for structured data management\n- `asyncio` for non-blocking cleanup operations\n\n## C. System Components\n\n### 1. RequestCleanupService\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Manage activity retention policies\n- Perform background cleanup\n- Provide filtering mechanisms\n\n**Key Methods:**\n- `configure_retention(default_period: timedelta)`\n- `filter_activities(criteria: Dict[str, Any]) -> List[Activity]`\n- `clear_request(request_id: str)`\n- `run_periodic_cleanup()`\n\n### 2. RetentionPolicyManager\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Define and enforce activity retention rules\n- Handle per-request and global retention configurations\n- Determine activity eligibility for deletion\n\n### 3. ActivityFilter\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Support complex query operations\n- Provide efficient activity retrieval and filtering\n- Minimize performance overhead\n\n## D. Data Model\n\n### Activity Metadata Structure\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass ActivityMetadata:\n    request_id: str\n    timestamp: datetime\n    retention_period: Optional[timedelta] = None\n    is_active: bool = False\n```\n\n## E. Detailed Design\n\n### Cleanup Algorithm Pseudocode\n```python\nasync def cleanup_activities():\n    for activity in get_expired_activities():\n        if not is_active_request(activity):\n            safe_delete(activity)\n```\n\n### Filtering Mechanism\n```python\ndef filter_activities(\n    request_id: Optional[str] = None,\n    start_time: Optional[datetime] = None,\n    end_time: Optional[datetime] = None,\n    active_only: bool = False\n) -> List[Activity]:\n    # Implement flexible, efficient filtering\n```\n\n## F. Configuration Options\n\n### Retention Policy Configuration\n```python\nclass RetentionConfig:\n    default_period: timedelta = timedelta(days=7)\n    max_retention_period: timedelta = timedelta(days=30)\n    cleanup_interval: timedelta = timedelta(hours=1)\n```\n\n## G. Deployment Strategy\n\n### Integration Points\n- Integrate with existing `activity_tracker.py`\n- Minimal changes to external API\n- Background task managed via `asyncio`\n\n## H. Testing Strategy\n\n### Test Coverage\n- Unit tests for each component\n- Integration tests for cleanup mechanism\n- Performance benchmarks\n- Edge case scenarios (partial data, race conditions)\n\n### Property-Based Testing\n- Use `hypothesis` to generate complex test scenarios\n- Verify data integrity during cleanup\n- Validate performance characteristics\n\n## I. Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Risk 1: Incomplete Data Removal\n**Mitigation:**\n- Implement comprehensive logging\n- Use transactional delete operations\n- Maintain rollback capabilities\n\n### Risk 2: Performance Overhead\n**Mitigation:**\n- Use async processing\n- Implement efficient indexing\n- Configure tunable cleanup intervals\n\n## J. Alternatives Considered\n\n### Alternative 1: Full Rebuild\n**Pros:** Complete redesign\n**Cons:** High risk, significant effort\n**Verdict:** Rejected in favor of incremental improvement\n\n### Alternative 2: Time-Based Deletion\n**Pros:** Simple implementation\n**Cons:** Less granular control\n**Verdict:** Partial adoption with enhanced filtering\n\n## K. Open Questions for Stakeholder\n\n1. Desired default retention period beyond 7 days?\n2. Specific performance requirements for cleanup operations?\n3. Logging and audit trail expectations for deleted activities?\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThis architecture provides a robust, flexible solution for request cleanup while maintaining system performance and data integrity.\n\n**Key Design Principles:**\n- Minimal invasiveness\n- Configurability\n- Async, non-blocking design\n- Comprehensive error handling'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VtbfNpEd1oEmLq2CopxjbU', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260115_014706.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260115_014706.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01YH4JkUpTJfUSexzXQu2gdc', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Request Cleanup System Improvement', 'description': "Enhance ActivityTracker's request cleanup mechanism to resolve memory growth issues and implement robust activity filtering."}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01YH4JkUpTJfUSexzXQu2gdc', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "79f57612", "message": "Created project: Request Cleanup System Improvement", "summary": {"project_id": "79f57612", "project_name": "Request Cleanup System Improvement", "description": "Enhance ActivityTracker\'s request cleanup mechanism to resolve memory growth issues and implement robust activity filtering.", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-15T01:47:09.728669", "updated_at": "2026-01-15T01:47:09.728669", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-15T01:47:09.728669", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Request Cleanup System Improvement\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.6\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully analyzed the complex UI enhancement requirements and designed a focused, performance-oriented architecture that leverages existing React patterns while adding sophisticated dynamic filt...\n- I successfully analyzed the token tracking requirements and designed a risk-minimal architecture that enhances the existing pipeline without breaking changes. The proposal balances comprehensive funct...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description':