{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 01:48:21", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-2627fa81-c5bb-4dee-9596-1a81ea10e26f', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Filtering and Basic Cleanup Foundation",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md",\n  "target_file": "src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01B7XtSGdogHHzVnjMkTWQGQ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RduGUGY81h2RVnMTUhAsrN', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01WUs55CQmwJLYUcYeqCN74Y', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_018zLjTfSn6STaoYrmx9whbe', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01B7XtSGdogHHzVnjMkTWQGQ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Request Cleanup System Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Design Pattern: Enhanced Service Module with Background Processing\\nThe Request Cleanup System will be implemented as an enhanced service module within the existing ActivityTracker, leveraging a modular, configurable approach to activity management and cleanup.\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **Concurrency**: `asyncio` for background processing\\n- **Testing**: `pytest` with `hypothesis` for property-based testing\\n\\n### Key Libraries\\n- `typing` for type hints\\n- `dataclasses` for structured data management\\n- `asyncio` for non-blocking cleanup operations\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n### 1. RequestCleanupService\\n**Responsibilities:**\\n- Manage activity retention policies\\n- Perform background cleanup\\n- Provide filtering mechanisms\\n\\n**Key Methods:**\\n- `configure_retention(default_period: timedelta)`\\n- `filter_activities(criteria: Dict[str, Any]) -> List[Activity]`\\n- `clear_request(request_id: str)`\\n- `run_periodic_cleanup()`\\n\\n### 2. RetentionPolicyManager\\n**Responsibilities:**\\n- Define and enforce activity retention rules\\n- Handle per-request and global retention configurations\\n- Determine activity eligibility for deletion\\n\\n### 3. ActivityFilter\\n**Responsibilities:**\\n- Support complex query operations\\n- Provide efficient activity retrieval and filtering\\n- Minimize performance overhead\\n\\n## D. Data Model\\n\\n### Activity Metadata Structure\\n```python\\n@dataclass\\nclass ActivityMetadata:\\n    request_id: str\\n    timestamp: datetime\\n    retention_period: Optional[timedelta] = None\\n    is_active: bool = False\\n```\\n\\n## E. Detailed Design\\n\\n### Cleanup Algorithm Pseudocode\\n```python\\nasync def cleanup_activities():\\n    for activity in get_expired_activities():\\n        if not is_active_request(activity):\\n            safe_delete(activity)\\n```\\n\\n### Filtering Mechanism\\n```python\\ndef filter_activities(\\n    request_id: Optional[str] = None,\\n    start_time: Optional[datetime] = None,\\n    end_time: Optional[datetime] = None,\\n    active_only: bool = False\\n) -> List[Activity]:\\n    # Implement flexible, efficient filtering\\n```\\n\\n## F. Configuration Options\\n\\n### Retention Policy Configuration\\n```python\\nclass RetentionConfig:\\n    default_period: timedelta = timedelta(days=7)\\n    max_retention_period: timedelta = timedelta(days=30)\\n    cleanup_interval: timedelta = timedelta(hours=1)\\n```\\n\\n## G. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Integration Points\\n- Integrate with existing `activity_tracker.py`\\n- Minimal changes to external API\\n- Background task managed via `asyncio`\\n\\n## H. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Test Coverage\\n- Unit tests for each component\\n- Integration tests for cleanup mechanism\\n- Performance benchmarks\\n- Edge case scenarios (partial data, race conditions)\\n\\n### Property-Based Testing\\n- Use `hypothesis` to generate complex test scenarios\\n- Verify data integrity during cleanup\\n- Validate performance characteristics\\n\\n## I. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Incomplete Data Removal\\n**Mitigation:**\\n- Implement comprehensive logging\\n- Use transactional delete operations\\n- Maintain rollback capabilities\\n\\n### Risk 2: Performance Overhead\\n**Mitigation:**\\n- Use async processing\\n- Implement efficient indexing\\n- Configure tunable cleanup intervals\\n\\n## J. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Full Rebuild\\n**Pros:** Complete redesign\\n**Cons:** High risk, significant effort\\n**Verdict:** Rejected in favor of incremental improvement\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Time-Based Deletion\\n**Pros:** Simple implementation\\n**Cons:** Less granular control\\n**Verdict:** Partial adoption with enhanced filtering\\n\\n## K. Open Questions for Stakeholder\\n\\n1. Desired default retention period beyond 7 days?\\n2. Specific performance requirements for cleanup operations?\\n3. Logging and audit trail expectations for deleted activities?\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a robust, flexible solution for request cleanup while maintaining system performance and data integrity.\\n\\n**Key Design Principles:**\\n- Minimal invasiveness\\n- Configurability\\n- Async, non-blocking design\\n- Comprehensive error handling"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RduGUGY81h2RVnMTUhAsrN', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Request Cleanup System Improvement Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nEnhance the ActivityTracker\'s request cleanup mechanism to resolve memory growth issues and implement robust activity filtering.\\n\\n## Context\\n- Current `clear_request()` method in ActivityTracker is incomplete\\n- No effective request filtering mechanism exists\\n- Activities accumulate without proper cleanup\\n- Causing significant memory usage growth\\n\\n## Detailed Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Request Cleanup Implementation\\n- Complete `clear_request()` method in `activity_tracker.py`\\n- Fully remove request-specific data from tracking system\\n- Ensure no orphaned or partial data remains\\n\\n### 2. Activity Filtering\\n- Implement filtering mechanism by `request_id`\\n- Allow selective retrieval and deletion of activities\\n- Support complex query operations on activity metadata\\n\\n### 3. Automatic Cleanup Mechanism\\n- Add configurable activity retention policy\\n- Automatically remove activities older than specified threshold\\n- Configurable retention period (default and per-request)\\n- Preserve active request data during cleanup\\n\\n### 4. Performance and Stability\\n- Maintain system performance during cleanup operations\\n- Prevent memory leaks\\n- Minimal performance overhead\\n- Ensure cleanup does not interrupt ongoing activities\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- \\u2705 `clear_request()` completely removes request data\\n- \\u2705 Implement robust activity filtering by `request_id`\\n- \\u2705 Automatic cleanup of old activities\\n- \\u2705 Configurable retention periods\\n- \\u2705 Memory usage remains stable\\n- \\u2705 No data loss for active requests\\n- \\u2705 Existing system functionality unaffected\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Modify: `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\\n- TDD Approach: Write tests first, then implementation\\n- Maintain backward compatibility\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Retention period will be configurable (default: 7 days)\\n- Cleanup will run as background task\\n- No performance degradation during cleanup\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Complete system rewrite\\n- Changes to external API\\n- Modifications to unrelated tracking components\\n\\n## Potential Risks\\n- Incomplete data removal\\n- Performance impact during cleanup\\n- Unintended data loss\\n\\n## Recommended Approach\\n1. Write comprehensive test cases\\n2. Implement filtering mechanism\\n3. Develop cleanup algorithm\\n4. Add configuration options\\n5. Perform extensive performance testing"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01WUs55CQmwJLYUcYeqCN74Y', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Test Strategy - Dynamic Activity Feed Enhancement\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis test strategy covers comprehensive testing for the Dynamic Activity Feed Enhancement milestone, which replaces hardcoded activity filters with dynamic generation based on actual activity data and semantic groupings.\\n\\n## Test Architecture\\n\\n### Test Pyramid\\n- **Unit Tests (80% coverage)**: Pure logic, utilities, hooks\\n- **Integration Tests (100% API coverage)**: Component interactions, data flow\\n- **End-to-End Tests**: Critical user workflows\\n\\n### Testing Framework Stack\\n- **Unit Tests**: Jest + React Testing Library\\n- **Integration Tests**: Jest + Mock Service Worker (MSW)\\n- **E2E Tests**: Playwright for cross-browser testing\\n- **Performance Tests**: Jest + React Testing Library performance utilities\\n\\n## Unit Test Coverage\\n\\n### 1. Activity Analysis & Filter Generation Logic\\n**File**: `utils/activityCategorizer.test.js`\\n**Coverage Goal**: 95%\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Categorize activities into semantic groups\\n- Handle unknown activity types (fallback to \\"Other\\")\\n- Map activity types to correct categories\\n- Generate activity counts per category\\n- Handle empty activity arrays\\n- Handle malformed activity data\\n\\n**File**: `utils/filterGenerator.test.js`\\n**Coverage Goal**: 95%\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Generate filter options from activity data\\n- Create semantic groupings correctly\\n- Include activity counts in filter options\\n- Handle edge cases (no activities, single activity type)\\n- Generate icons and labels for categories\\n- Filter duplicate activity types\\n\\n**File**: `utils/agentTypeDetector.test.js`\\n**Coverage Goal**: 95%\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Detect all unique agent types from activities\\n- Categorize agents into roles (Leadership, Development, Testing)\\n- Track newly discovered agent types\\n- Handle agents without explicit type information\\n- Extract agent names from activity data\\n\\n### 2. Custom Hooks Testing\\n**File**: `hooks/useActivityAnalyzer.test.js`\\n**Coverage Goal**: 90%\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Analyze activities and return categorized data\\n- Update analysis when activities change\\n- Memoize results for performance\\n- Handle large activity datasets efficiently\\n- Return correct activity counts per category\\n\\n**File**: `hooks/useDynamicFilters.test.js`\\n**Coverage Goal**: 90%\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Generate filters from activities\\n- Apply selected filters to activity list\\n- Update filters when new activity types appear\\n- Handle filter selection/deselection\\n- Maintain filter state across re-renders\\n- Performance with 500+ activities\\n\\n**File**: `hooks/useAgentTypeRegistry.test.js`\\n**Coverage Goal**: 90%\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Track discovered agent types\\n- Categorize agent types correctly\\n- Detect new agent types in real-time\\n- Maintain agent type registry state\\n- Return agent type metrics\\n\\n**File**: `hooks/useErrorStateTracker.test.js`\\n**Coverage Goal**: 90%\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Detect error activities and failed agents\\n- Track error patterns over time\\n- Highlight problematic agents\\n- Return error state summary\\n- Handle different error activity formats\\n\\n### 3. Component Unit Tests\\n**File**: `components/DynamicActivityFilter.test.jsx`\\n**Coverage Goal**: 85%\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Render filter options dynamically\\n- Handle filter selection events\\n- Display activity counts correctly\\n- Show/hide semantic groupings\\n- Handle empty filter lists\\n- Accessibility compliance (ARIA labels)\\n\\n**File**: `components/FilterOptionGenerator.test.jsx`\\n**Coverage Goal**: 85%\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Generate UI-ready filter options\\n- Handle category grouping display\\n- Show activity counts in labels\\n- Render appropriate icons\\n- Handle user interactions\\n\\n**File**: `components/ActivityCategorizer.test.jsx`\\n**Coverage Goal**: 85%\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Apply category styles correctly\\n- Handle unknown activity types\\n- Display category badges\\n- Show activity metadata\\n\\n**File**: `components/AgentTypeDetector.test.jsx`\\n**Coverage Goal**: 85%\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Display discovered agent types\\n- Show new agent type notifications\\n- Handle agent type categorization\\n- Update when new types appear\\n\\n**File**: `components/ErrorStateHighlighter.test.jsx`\\n**Coverage Goal**: 85%\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Highlight error states visually\\n- Show error details on interaction\\n- Display failed agent indicators\\n- Apply appropriate error styling\\n\\n## Integration Test Coverage\\n\\n### 1. Component Integration Tests\\n**File**: `integration/ActivityFeedIntegration.test.jsx`\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Activity feed updates filters when activities change\\n- Filter selection correctly filters activity list\\n- New activity types appear in filters automatically\\n- Activity counts update in real-time\\n- Error states trigger visual highlighting\\n- Performance with rapid activity updates\\n\\n### 2. Hook Integration Tests\\n**File**: `integration/FilterSystemIntegration.test.js`\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Multiple hooks work together correctly\\n- Activity analysis feeds into filter generation\\n- Agent type detection integrates with metrics\\n- Error tracking works with activity filtering\\n- State updates propagate across hook system\\n\\n### 3. Context Integration Tests\\n**File**: `integration/FilterContextIntegration.test.jsx`\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Filter state shared across components\\n- Context updates trigger component re-renders\\n- Filter changes propagate to all consumers\\n- Performance with multiple context consumers\\n\\n### 4. Real-time Update Tests\\n**File**: `integration/RealTimeUpdates.test.jsx`\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- New activities trigger filter recalculation\\n- New agent types appear in UI within 1 second\\n- Activity counts update immediately\\n- Filter options maintain stability during updates\\n\\n## End-to-End Test Coverage\\n\\n### 1. Core User Workflows\\n**File**: `e2e/dynamicFiltering.spec.js`\\n\\n**Critical Path Tests**:\\n- User can see all activity types in filter dropdown\\n- Selecting filter shows only relevant activities\\n- New agent spawn appears in filters within 5 seconds\\n- Error activities are easily discoverable\\n- Activity counts match actual filtered results\\n- Filter state persists during navigation\\n\\n### 2. Agent Discovery Workflow\\n**File**: `e2e/agentDiscovery.spec.js`\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- New agent type appears in metrics pane\\n- Agent type filters work in agent states pane\\n- Failed agents are prominently highlighted\\n- Agent type distribution updates correctly\\n\\n### 3. Error Handling Workflow\\n**File**: `e2e/errorHandling.spec.js`\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Failed agents trigger error highlights\\n- Error filter shows only error activities\\n- Error states are visually distinct\\n- User can quickly identify system problems\\n\\n## Performance Test Coverage\\n\\n### 1. Filter Performance Tests\\n**File**: `performance/filterPerformance.test.js`\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Filter generation completes under 100ms for 500 activities\\n- Filter application under 50ms for any activity count\\n- Memory usage remains stable during extended filtering\\n- No memory leaks during repeated filter changes\\n\\n### 2. Real-time Update Performance\\n**File**: `performance/realTimePerformance.test.js`\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n- Activity addition triggers update within 200ms\\n- Filter recalculation doesn\'t block UI\\n- Component re-renders minimized during updates\\n- Large activity datasets don\'t degrade performance\\n\\n## Test Data & Fixtures\\n\\n### Mock Activity Data\\n```javascript\\n// fixtures/mockActivities.js\\nexport const MOCK_ACTIVITIES = [\\n  {\\n    activity_type: \'agent_spawned\',\\n    agent_name: \'Code Writer\',\\n    timestamp: \'2024-01-01T10:00:00Z\',\\n    status: \'success\'\\n  },\\n  {\\n    activity_type: \'tool_use_failed\',\\n    agent_name: \'System Architect\',\\n    timestamp: \'2024-01-01T10:01:00Z\',\\n    status: \'error\',\\n    error_details: \'Network timeout\'\\n  }\\n  // ... additional test data\\n]\\n```\\n\\n### Agent Type Test Data\\n```javascript\\n// fixtures/mockAgentTypes.js\\nexport const MOCK_AGENT_TYPES = {\\n  \'Executive Director\': { category: \'Leadership\', performance: 0.95 },\\n  \'Code Writer\': { category: \'Development\', performance: 0.88 },\\n  \'TDD Coordinator\': { category: \'Testing\', performance: 0.92 }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Test Environment Setup\\n\\n### Test Configuration\\n```javascript\\n// jest.config.js additions\\nmodule.exports = {\\n  testEnvironment: \'jsdom\',\\n  setupFilesAfterEnv: [\'<rootDir>/src/test/setupTests.js\'],\\n  collectCoverageFrom: [\\n    \'src/hooks/**/*.js\',\\n    \'src/utils/**/*.js\',\\n    \'src/components/**/*.{js,jsx}\',\\n    \'!src/**/*.test.{js,jsx}\',\\n    \'!src/**/index.js\'\\n  ],\\n  coverageThreshold: {\\n    global: {\\n      branches: 80,\\n      functions: 80,\\n      lines: 80,\\n      statements: 80\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Mock Service Worker Setup\\n```javascript\\n// mocks/handlers.js\\nexport const handlers = [\\n  rest.get(\'/api/activities\', (req, res, ctx) => {\\n    return res(ctx.json(MOCK_ACTIVITIES))\\n  }),\\n  rest.get(\'/api/agents\', (req, res, ctx) => {\\n    return res(ctx.json(MOCK_AGENTS))\\n  })\\n]\\n```\\n\\n## Continuous Integration\\n\\n### GitHub Actions Test Pipeline\\n```yaml\\n# .github/workflows/test.yml\\nname: Test Dynamic Filter Enhancement\\non: [push, pull_request]\\njobs:\\n  test:\\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n    steps:\\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\\n      - name: Setup Node.js\\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v3\\n        with:\\n          node-version: \'18\'\\n      - name: Install dependencies\\n        run: npm ci\\n      - name: Run unit tests\\n        run: npm run test:unit -- --coverage\\n      - name: Run integration tests  \\n        run: npm run test:integration\\n      - name: Run E2E tests\\n        run: npm run test:e2e\\n      - name: Upload coverage\\n        uses: codecov/codecov-action@v3\\n```\\n\\n## Test Execution Strategy\\n\\n### Development Testing\\n1. **TDD Approach**: Write tests before implementing features\\n2. **Fast Feedback**: Unit tests run on save during development\\n3. **Integration Testing**: Run before each commit\\n4. **Manual Testing**: E2E tests during feature completion\\n\\n### Pre-deployment Testing\\n1. **Full Test Suite**: All tests must pass\\n2. **Performance Validation**: Performance tests with large datasets\\n3. **Browser Compatibility**: E2E tests across Chrome, Firefox, Safari\\n4. **Accessibility Testing**: Screen reader and keyboard navigation\\n\\n### Post-deployment Monitoring\\n1. **Real User Monitoring**: Track filter usage patterns\\n2. **Error Monitoring**: Monitor for filter-related JavaScript errors\\n3. **Performance Monitoring**: Track filter performance in production\\n4. **User Feedback**: Collect feedback on filter usability\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n### Test Coverage Goals\\n- **Unit Tests**: 80%+ line coverage, 90%+ for critical paths\\n- **Integration Tests**: 100% component interaction coverage\\n- **E2E Tests**: 100% critical user workflow coverage\\n\\n### Performance Benchmarks\\n- **Filter Generation**: <100ms for 500 activities\\n- **Filter Application**: <50ms for any dataset size\\n- **UI Responsiveness**: No blocking operations >100ms\\n\\n### Quality Gates\\n- **All tests pass**: Zero failing tests\\n- **No performance regressions**: Current benchmarks maintained\\n- **Accessibility compliance**: WCAG 2.1 AA standards met\\n- **Cross-browser compatibility**: Works in Chrome, Firefox, Safari\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n\\n### Test Environment Risks\\n- **Mock data accuracy**: Regularly update mocks with real activity patterns\\n- **Test isolation**: Ensure tests don\'t interfere with each other\\n- **Flaky tests**: Implement retry mechanisms for timing-dependent tests\\n\\n### Performance Testing Risks\\n- **Real-world conditions**: Test with realistic data volumes and patterns\\n- **Memory leak detection**: Monitor memory usage during long test runs\\n- **Concurrency issues**: Test multiple simultaneous filter operations\\n\\n### Browser Compatibility Risks\\n- **Feature detection**: Test unsupported browser graceful degradation\\n- **Polyfill testing**: Verify polyfills work correctly\\n- **Mobile testing**: Include mobile browser testing in E2E suite\\""}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_018zLjTfSn6STaoYrmx9whbe', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "File not found: /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py